<https://w3id.org/project-chemie-digital/graph/scenes/level8-linear-regression> {
  ex:l8-item-01-1 a cd:SceneItem ; cd:position 1 ; cd:language "en" ; cd:selectsResource ex:l8-heading-01 ; cd:communicativeRole cd:HeadingRole ; cd:selectionPath "skos:prefLabel@en" ; cd:authoredResource true .
  ex:l8-scene-01 a cd:SceneDefinition ; cd:focusConcept ex:l8-linear-regression ; cd:teachingSceneType cd:TitleSlide ; cd:narration "Today we turn a time trend into a reproducible fitted model. We first agree what a good line means, then acquire enough matrix language to build a design matrix and derive the normal equations. The final applications change the known model terms without changing the linear coefficient problem. Uncertainty belongs to the next appointment."@en ; cd:hasSceneItem ex:l8-item-01-1 ; cd:authoredResource true .
  ex:l8-scene-01 cd:hasSource ex:l8-source-author .
  ex:l8-item-02-1 a cd:SceneItem ; cd:position 1 ; cd:language "en" ; cd:selectsResource ex:l8-heading-02 ; cd:communicativeRole cd:HeadingRole ; cd:selectionPath "skos:prefLabel@en" ; cd:authoredResource true .
  ex:l8-item-02-2 a cd:SceneItem ; cd:position 2 ; cd:language "en" ; cd:selectsResource ex:l8-media-detector-drift-use-case ; cd:communicativeRole cd:MediaRole ; cd:selectionPath "cd:uri" ; cd:authoredResource true .
  ex:l8-item-02-3 a cd:SceneItem ; cd:position 3 ; cd:language "en" ; cd:selectsResource ex:l8-essence-02 ; cd:communicativeRole cd:StatementRole ; cd:selectionPath "cd:body" ; cd:authoredResource true .
  ex:l8-item-02-4 a cd:SceneItem ; cd:position 4 ; cd:language "en" ; cd:selectsResource ex:l8-heading-03 ; cd:communicativeRole cd:StatementRole ; cd:selectionPath "cd:body" ; cd:revealOn ex:l8-media-detector-drift-use-case ; cd:revealAtStage 1 ; cd:authoredResource true .
  ex:l8-scene-02 a cd:SceneDefinition ; cd:focusConcept ex:l8-linear-regression ; cd:teachingSceneType cd:UseCaseSlide ; cd:narration "During one run, we recorded the detector signal at the start and then once per minute. Reveal the five readings, then mark 2.5 min between two observed times. Ask learners to estimate the missing signal in mV. Then show a candidate line as a mathematical description: we can evaluate it between readings or extend it beyond the measured range. A dashed extension marks extrapolation. Ask what makes one line a better model for these data than another."@en ; cd:hasSceneItem ex:l8-item-02-1, ex:l8-item-02-2, ex:l8-item-02-3, ex:l8-item-02-4 ; cd:authoredResource true .
  ex:l8-scene-02 cd:hasSource ex:l8-source-author .
  ex:l8-item-estimate-line-1 a cd:SceneItem ; cd:position 1 ; cd:language "en" ; cd:selectsResource ex:l8-heading-estimate-line-coefficients ; cd:communicativeRole cd:HeadingRole ; cd:selectionPath "skos:prefLabel@en" ; cd:authoredResource true .
  ex:l8-item-estimate-line-2 a cd:SceneItem ; cd:position 2 ; cd:language "en" ; cd:selectsResource ex:l8-media-estimate-line-coefficients ; cd:communicativeRole cd:MediaRole ; cd:selectionPath "cd:uri" ; cd:authoredResource true .
  ex:l8-item-estimate-line-3 a cd:SceneItem ; cd:position 3 ; cd:language "en" ; cd:selectsResource ex:l8-essence-estimate-line-coefficients ; cd:communicativeRole cd:StatementRole ; cd:selectionPath "cd:body" ; cd:authoredResource true .
  ex:l8-scene-estimate-line-coefficients a cd:SceneDefinition ; cd:focusConcept ex:l8-linear-regression ; cd:teachingSceneType cd:InterpretationSlide ; cd:narration "Once we choose a straight-line model, two numbers are still unknown. The intercept gives the modelled signal at zero minutes. The slope gives the modelled change in signal per minute. We use all five measured pairs to estimate both together. Next, try adjusting the intercept and slope yourself."@en ; cd:hasSceneItem ex:l8-item-estimate-line-1, ex:l8-item-estimate-line-2, ex:l8-item-estimate-line-3 ; cd:authoredResource true .
  ex:l8-scene-estimate-line-coefficients cd:hasSource ex:l8-source-author .
  ex:l8-item-04-1 a cd:SceneItem ; cd:position 1 ; cd:language "en" ; cd:selectsResource ex:l8-heading-04 ; cd:communicativeRole cd:HeadingRole ; cd:selectionPath "skos:prefLabel@en" ; cd:authoredResource true .
  ex:l8-item-04-2 a cd:SceneItem ; cd:position 2 ; cd:language "en" ; cd:selectsResource ex:l8-fit-drift-manual ; cd:communicativeRole cd:ChartRole ; cd:selectionPath "cd:body" ; cd:authoredResource true .
  ex:l8-item-04-3 a cd:SceneItem ; cd:position 3 ; cd:language "en" ; cd:selectsResource ex:l8-f-line ; cd:communicativeRole cd:FormulaRole ; cd:selectionPath "cd:latex" ; cd:authoredResource true .
  ex:l8-item-04-4 a cd:SceneItem ; cd:position 4 ; cd:language "en" ; cd:selectsResource ex:l8-essence-04 ; cd:communicativeRole cd:StatementRole ; cd:selectionPath "cd:body" ; cd:authoredResource true .
  ex:l8-scene-04 a cd:SceneDefinition ; cd:focusConcept ex:l8-linear-regression ; cd:teachingSceneType cd:ExplorationSlide ; cd:narration "Start with the two controls and ask what makes one line fit better than another. Reveal the residual bar chart. Each bar shows the measured signal minus the prediction at the same time. Move the intercept and slope, and match each vertical gap in the scatter plot to its bar. A point above the line gives a bar above zero. A point below the line gives a bar below zero."@en ; cd:hasSceneItem ex:l8-item-04-1, ex:l8-item-04-2, ex:l8-item-04-3, ex:l8-item-04-4 ; cd:authoredResource true .
  ex:l8-scene-04 cd:hasSource ex:l8-source-author .
  ex:l8-scene-04 dct:references ex:l8-fit-drift-manual .
  ex:l8-item-05-1 a cd:SceneItem ; cd:position 1 ; cd:language "en" ; cd:selectsResource ex:l8-heading-05 ; cd:communicativeRole cd:HeadingRole ; cd:selectionPath "skos:prefLabel@en" ; cd:authoredResource true .
  ex:l8-item-05-2 a cd:SceneItem ; cd:position 2 ; cd:language "en" ; cd:selectsResource ex:l8-media-drift-residuals ; cd:communicativeRole cd:MediaRole ; cd:selectionPath "cd:uri" ; cd:authoredResource true .
  ex:l8-item-05-3 a cd:SceneItem ; cd:position 3 ; cd:language "en" ; cd:selectsResource ex:l8-f-residual ; cd:communicativeRole cd:FormulaRole ; cd:selectionPath "cd:latex" ; cd:authoredResource true .
  ex:l8-item-05-4 a cd:SceneItem ; cd:position 4 ; cd:language "en" ; cd:selectsResource ex:l8-essence-05 ; cd:communicativeRole cd:StatementRole ; cd:selectionPath "cd:body" ; cd:revealOn ex:l8-media-drift-residuals ; cd:revealAtStage 2 ; cd:authoredResource true .
  ex:l8-scene-05 a cd:SceneDefinition ; cd:focusConcept ex:l8-linear-regression ; cd:teachingSceneType cd:InterpretationSlide ; cd:narration "At the fitted drift line, compute each observation minus its prediction at exactly the same time. A point above the line has positive residual; one below has negative residual. The staged stems show +0.08, −0.21, +0.20, −0.09, +0.02 mV. These are vertical signal gaps, not perpendicular geometric distances."@en ; cd:hasSceneItem ex:l8-item-05-1, ex:l8-item-05-2, ex:l8-item-05-3, ex:l8-item-05-4 ; cd:authoredResource true .
  ex:l8-scene-05 cd:hasSource ex:l8-source-author .
  ex:l8-item-06-1 a cd:SceneItem ; cd:position 1 ; cd:language "en" ; cd:selectsResource ex:l8-heading-06 ; cd:communicativeRole cd:HeadingRole ; cd:selectionPath "skos:prefLabel@en" ; cd:authoredResource true .
  ex:l8-item-06-2 a cd:SceneItem ; cd:position 2 ; cd:language "en" ; cd:selectsResource ex:l8-media-signed-gaps-question ; cd:communicativeRole cd:MediaRole ; cd:selectionPath "cd:uri" ; cd:authoredResource true .
  ex:l8-item-06-3 a cd:SceneItem ; cd:position 3 ; cd:language "en" ; cd:selectsResource ex:l8-essence-06 ; cd:communicativeRole cd:StatementRole ; cd:selectionPath "cd:body" ; cd:revealOn ex:l8-media-signed-gaps-question ; cd:revealAtStage 1 ; cd:authoredResource true .
  ex:l8-scene-06 a cd:SceneDefinition ; cd:focusConcept ex:l8-linear-regression ; cd:teachingSceneType cd:ExplorationSlide ; cd:narration "Read the five signed residuals and ask what happens when they are added. Reveal their total, 0.00 mV. Each point still misses the fitted line: positive and negative gaps cancel. The next slide introduces a score that counts gaps on both sides."@en ; cd:hasSceneItem ex:l8-item-06-1, ex:l8-item-06-2, ex:l8-item-06-3 ; cd:authoredResource true .
  ex:l8-scene-06 cd:hasSource ex:l8-source-author .
  ex:l8-item-07-1 a cd:SceneItem ; cd:position 1 ; cd:language "en" ; cd:selectsResource ex:l8-heading-07 ; cd:communicativeRole cd:HeadingRole ; cd:selectionPath "skos:prefLabel@en" ; cd:authoredResource true .
  ex:l8-item-07-2 a cd:SceneItem ; cd:position 2 ; cd:language "en" ; cd:selectsResource ex:l8-media-compare-residual-scores ; cd:communicativeRole cd:MediaRole ; cd:selectionPath "cd:uri" ; cd:authoredResource true .
  ex:l8-item-07-3 a cd:SceneItem ; cd:position 3 ; cd:language "en" ; cd:selectsResource ex:l8-f-criterion ; cd:communicativeRole cd:FormulaRole ; cd:selectionPath "cd:latex" ; cd:revealOn ex:l8-media-compare-residual-scores ; cd:revealAtStage 2 ; cd:authoredResource true .
  ex:l8-item-07-4 a cd:SceneItem ; cd:position 4 ; cd:language "en" ; cd:selectsResource ex:l8-essence-07 ; cd:communicativeRole cd:StatementRole ; cd:selectionPath "cd:body" ; cd:revealOn ex:l8-media-compare-residual-scores ; cd:revealAtStage 2 ; cd:authoredResource true .
  ex:l8-scene-07 a cd:SceneDefinition ; cd:focusConcept ex:l8-linear-regression ; cd:teachingSceneType cd:InterpretationSlide ; cd:narration "Compare two lines against the same five measurements. Ask which would get the smaller score by adding residuals as they are. Both sums are zero because the positive and negative gaps cancel. Reveal the squared sums: 2.70 for the line we started with and 0.10 for the closer candidate. Squaring prevents cancellation and makes a gap twice as large count four times as much. Choose coefficients that minimise this total. Absolute gaps also avoid cancellation. The squared score is smooth in the coefficients, which will let us derive equations for the minimum."@en ; cd:hasSceneItem ex:l8-item-07-1, ex:l8-item-07-2, ex:l8-item-07-3, ex:l8-item-07-4 ; cd:authoredResource true .
  ex:l8-scene-07 cd:hasSource ex:l8-source-nist-ls .
  ex:l8-minimum-two-coefficients-item-1 a cd:SceneItem ; cd:position 1 ; cd:language "en" ; cd:selectsResource ex:l8-minimum-two-coefficients-heading ; cd:communicativeRole cd:HeadingRole ; cd:selectionPath "skos:prefLabel@en" ; cd:authoredResource true .
  ex:l8-minimum-two-coefficients-item-2 a cd:SceneItem ; cd:position 2 ; cd:language "en" ; cd:selectsResource ex:l8-fit-drift-local-objective ; cd:communicativeRole cd:ChartRole ; cd:selectionPath "cd:body" ; cd:authoredResource true .
  ex:l8-minimum-two-coefficients-item-4 a cd:SceneItem ; cd:position 3 ; cd:language "en" ; cd:selectsResource ex:l8-minimum-two-coefficients-takeaway ; cd:communicativeRole cd:StatementRole ; cd:selectionPath "cd:body" ; cd:authoredResource true .
  ex:l8-minimum-two-coefficients-scene a cd:SceneDefinition ; cd:focusConcept ex:l8-linear-regression ; cd:teachingSceneType cd:ExplorationSlide ; cd:narration "Move one slider at a time while keeping the measured points fixed. Each local error plot varies one coefficient while holding the other at its current setting. Look for a pair where both marked points lie at the bottoms of their curves."@en ; cd:hasSceneItem ex:l8-minimum-two-coefficients-item-1, ex:l8-minimum-two-coefficients-item-2, ex:l8-minimum-two-coefficients-item-4 ; cd:hasSource ex:l8-source-author ; cd:authoredResource true .
  ex:l8-squared-error-conditions-heading-item a cd:SceneItem ; cd:position 1 ; cd:language "en" ; cd:selectsResource ex:l8-squared-error-conditions-heading ; cd:communicativeRole cd:HeadingRole ; cd:selectionPath "skos:prefLabel@en" ; cd:authoredResource true .
  ex:l8-squared-error-conditions-formula-item a cd:SceneItem ; cd:position 2 ; cd:language "en" ; cd:selectsResource ex:l8-minimum-two-coefficients-formula ; cd:communicativeRole cd:FormulaRole ; cd:selectionPath "cd:latex" ; cd:authoredResource true .
  ex:l8-squared-error-conditions-scene a cd:SceneDefinition ; cd:focusConcept ex:l8-linear-regression ; cd:teachingSceneType cd:DerivationSlide ; cd:narration "Use the same five measurements. Q sums the squared residuals. The total differential gives the first-order change in Q for a small change in both coefficients. At the minimum this change vanishes in every direction. Varying each coefficient on its own gives the two zero-derivative conditions at the same pair."@en ; cd:hasSceneItem ex:l8-squared-error-conditions-heading-item, ex:l8-squared-error-conditions-formula-item ; cd:hasSource ex:l8-source-author ; cd:authoredResource true .
  ex:l8-item-08-1 a cd:SceneItem ; cd:position 1 ; cd:language "en" ; cd:selectsResource ex:l8-heading-08 ; cd:communicativeRole cd:HeadingRole ; cd:selectionPath "skos:prefLabel@en" ; cd:authoredResource true .
  ex:l8-scene-08 a cd:SceneDefinition ; cd:focusConcept ex:l8-linear-regression ; cd:teachingSceneType cd:ChapterSlide ; cd:narration "A short detour: read matrices, multiply them and use an inverse to solve equations."@en ; cd:hasSceneItem ex:l8-item-08-1 ; cd:authoredResource true .
  ex:l8-scene-08 cd:hasSource ex:l8-source-author .
  ex:l8-item-09-1 a cd:SceneItem ; cd:position 1 ; cd:language "en" ; cd:selectsResource ex:l8-heading-09 ; cd:communicativeRole cd:HeadingRole ; cd:selectionPath "skos:prefLabel@en" ; cd:authoredResource true .
  ex:l8-item-09-3 a cd:SceneItem ; cd:position 2 ; cd:language "en" ; cd:selectsResource ex:l8-f-shape ; cd:communicativeRole cd:FormulaRole ; cd:selectionPath "cd:latex" ; cd:authoredResource true .
  ex:l8-item-09-4 a cd:SceneItem ; cd:position 3 ; cd:language "en" ; cd:selectsResource ex:l8-essence-09 ; cd:communicativeRole cd:StatementRole ; cd:selectionPath "cd:body" ; cd:authoredResource true .
  ex:l8-scene-09 a cd:SceneDefinition ; cd:focusConcept ex:l8-linear-regression ; cd:teachingSceneType cd:InterpretationSlide ; cd:narration "Compare the 2 by 3, 3 by 2 and 2 by 4 arrays. Count horizontal rows first and vertical columns second. The first two arrays contain the same number of entries, but their shapes differ."@en ; cd:hasSceneItem ex:l8-item-09-1, ex:l8-item-09-3, ex:l8-item-09-4 ; cd:authoredResource true .
  ex:l8-scene-09 cd:hasSource ex:l8-source-author .
  ex:l8-item-10-1 a cd:SceneItem ; cd:position 1 ; cd:language "en" ; cd:selectsResource ex:l8-heading-10 ; cd:communicativeRole cd:HeadingRole ; cd:selectionPath "skos:prefLabel@en" ; cd:authoredResource true .
  ex:l8-item-10-3 a cd:SceneItem ; cd:position 2 ; cd:language "en" ; cd:selectsResource ex:l8-f-index ; cd:communicativeRole cd:FormulaRole ; cd:selectionPath "cd:latex" ; cd:authoredResource true .
  ex:l8-item-10-4 a cd:SceneItem ; cd:position 3 ; cd:language "en" ; cd:selectsResource ex:l8-essence-10 ; cd:communicativeRole cd:StatementRole ; cd:selectionPath "cd:body" ; cd:authoredResource true .
  ex:l8-scene-10 a cd:SceneDefinition ; cd:focusConcept ex:l8-linear-regression ; cd:teachingSceneType cd:InterpretationSlide ; cd:narration "Read a subscript pair in a fixed order. In the shown matrix, a subscript 23 means row 2 then column 3, so its value is 6. It does not mean row 3 column 2, and it does not mean the number twenty-three. The box marks the entry at that intersection."@en ; cd:hasSceneItem ex:l8-item-10-1, ex:l8-item-10-3, ex:l8-item-10-4 ; cd:authoredResource true .
  ex:l8-scene-10 cd:hasSource ex:l8-source-author .
  ex:l8-item-11-1 a cd:SceneItem ; cd:position 1 ; cd:language "en" ; cd:selectsResource ex:l8-heading-11 ; cd:communicativeRole cd:HeadingRole ; cd:selectionPath "skos:prefLabel@en" ; cd:authoredResource true .
  ex:l8-item-11-3 a cd:SceneItem ; cd:position 2 ; cd:language "en" ; cd:selectsResource ex:l8-f-vectors ; cd:communicativeRole cd:FormulaRole ; cd:selectionPath "cd:latex" ; cd:authoredResource true .
  ex:l8-item-11-4 a cd:SceneItem ; cd:position 3 ; cd:language "en" ; cd:selectsResource ex:l8-essence-11 ; cd:communicativeRole cd:StatementRole ; cd:selectionPath "cd:body" ; cd:authoredResource true .
  ex:l8-scene-11 a cd:SceneDefinition ; cd:focusConcept ex:l8-linear-regression ; cd:teachingSceneType cd:InterpretationSlide ; cd:narration "A column and a row can contain the same three entries. The same principle holds for larger matrices: transposing a 5 by 3 matrix gives a 3 by 5 matrix. The boxed first row becomes the boxed first column."@en ; cd:hasSceneItem ex:l8-item-11-1, ex:l8-item-11-3, ex:l8-item-11-4 ; cd:authoredResource true .
  ex:l8-scene-11 cd:hasSource ex:l8-source-author .
  ex:l8-item-12-1 a cd:SceneItem ; cd:position 1 ; cd:language "en" ; cd:selectsResource ex:l8-heading-12 ; cd:communicativeRole cd:HeadingRole ; cd:selectionPath "skos:prefLabel@en" ; cd:authoredResource true .
  ex:l8-item-12-2 a cd:SceneItem ; cd:position 2 ; cd:language "en" ; cd:selectsResource ex:l8-f-square ; cd:communicativeRole cd:FormulaRole ; cd:selectionPath "cd:latex" ; cd:authoredResource true .
  ex:l8-item-12-3 a cd:SceneItem ; cd:position 3 ; cd:language "en" ; cd:selectsResource ex:l8-essence-12 ; cd:communicativeRole cd:StatementRole ; cd:selectionPath "cd:body" ; cd:authoredResource true .
  ex:l8-scene-12 a cd:SceneDefinition ; cd:focusConcept ex:l8-linear-regression ; cd:teachingSceneType cd:InterpretationSlide ; cd:narration "Compare the 2 by 2, 3 by 3 and 4 by 4 examples. Every one is square because its row and column counts match. The positions and values of the entries can vary."@en ; cd:hasSceneItem ex:l8-item-12-1, ex:l8-item-12-2, ex:l8-item-12-3 ; cd:authoredResource true .
  ex:l8-scene-12 cd:hasSource ex:l8-source-author .
  ex:l8-item-13-1 a cd:SceneItem ; cd:position 1 ; cd:language "en" ; cd:selectsResource ex:l8-heading-13 ; cd:communicativeRole cd:HeadingRole ; cd:selectionPath "skos:prefLabel@en" ; cd:authoredResource true .
  ex:l8-item-13-2 a cd:SceneItem ; cd:position 2 ; cd:language "en" ; cd:selectsResource ex:l8-f-diagonal ; cd:communicativeRole cd:FormulaRole ; cd:selectionPath "cd:latex" ; cd:authoredResource true .
  ex:l8-item-13-3 a cd:SceneItem ; cd:position 3 ; cd:language "en" ; cd:selectsResource ex:l8-essence-13 ; cd:communicativeRole cd:StatementRole ; cd:selectionPath "cd:body" ; cd:authoredResource true .
  ex:l8-scene-13 a cd:SceneDefinition ; cd:focusConcept ex:l8-linear-regression ; cd:teachingSceneType cd:InterpretationSlide ; cd:narration "Compare diagonal matrices of sizes 2, 3 and 4. The highlighted diagonal is where the row and column indices agree. Every off-diagonal entry is zero. The 3 by 3 example has a zero on its main diagonal, which makes it singular."@en ; cd:hasSceneItem ex:l8-item-13-1, ex:l8-item-13-2, ex:l8-item-13-3 ; cd:authoredResource true .
  ex:l8-scene-13 cd:hasSource ex:l8-source-author .
  ex:l8-item-14-1 a cd:SceneItem ; cd:position 1 ; cd:language "en" ; cd:selectsResource ex:l8-heading-14 ; cd:communicativeRole cd:HeadingRole ; cd:selectionPath "skos:prefLabel@en" ; cd:authoredResource true .
  ex:l8-item-14-2 a cd:SceneItem ; cd:position 2 ; cd:language "en" ; cd:selectsResource ex:l8-f-identity ; cd:communicativeRole cd:FormulaRole ; cd:selectionPath "cd:latex" ; cd:authoredResource true .
  ex:l8-item-14-3 a cd:SceneItem ; cd:position 3 ; cd:language "en" ; cd:selectsResource ex:l8-essence-14 ; cd:communicativeRole cd:StatementRole ; cd:selectionPath "cd:body" ; cd:authoredResource true .
  ex:l8-scene-14 a cd:SceneDefinition ; cd:focusConcept ex:l8-linear-regression ; cd:teachingSceneType cd:InterpretationSlide ; cd:narration "Compare the identities of sizes 1, 2 and 3. Every diagonal entry is one. The left identity for a 2 by 3 matrix must have size 2, and the right identity must have size 3. Both products preserve the same matrix A."@en ; cd:hasSceneItem ex:l8-item-14-1, ex:l8-item-14-2, ex:l8-item-14-3 ; cd:authoredResource true .
  ex:l8-scene-14 cd:hasSource ex:l8-source-author .
  ex:l8-item-15-1 a cd:SceneItem ; cd:position 1 ; cd:language "en" ; cd:selectsResource ex:l8-heading-15 ; cd:communicativeRole cd:HeadingRole ; cd:selectionPath "skos:prefLabel@en" ; cd:authoredResource true .
  ex:l8-item-15-2 a cd:SceneItem ; cd:position 2 ; cd:language "en" ; cd:selectsResource ex:l8-f-add ; cd:communicativeRole cd:FormulaRole ; cd:selectionPath "cd:latex" ; cd:authoredResource true .
  ex:l8-item-15-3 a cd:SceneItem ; cd:position 3 ; cd:language "en" ; cd:selectsResource ex:l8-essence-15 ; cd:communicativeRole cd:StatementRole ; cd:selectionPath "cd:body" ; cd:authoredResource true .
  ex:l8-scene-15 a cd:SceneDefinition ; cd:focusConcept ex:l8-linear-regression ; cd:teachingSceneType cd:InterpretationSlide ; cd:narration "Both matrices have the same shape. Read the top-left cells first: add 1 and 5 or subtract 5 from 1. Then do the same at each of the other three positions. The result keeps the original shape. When entries have units, the two values being combined must have compatible units."@en ; cd:hasSceneItem ex:l8-item-15-1, ex:l8-item-15-2, ex:l8-item-15-3 ; cd:authoredResource true .
  ex:l8-scene-15 cd:hasSource ex:l8-source-author .
  ex:l8-item-16-1 a cd:SceneItem ; cd:position 1 ; cd:language "en" ; cd:selectsResource ex:l8-heading-16 ; cd:communicativeRole cd:HeadingRole ; cd:selectionPath "skos:prefLabel@en" ; cd:authoredResource true .
  ex:l8-item-16-2 a cd:SceneItem ; cd:position 2 ; cd:language "en" ; cd:selectsResource ex:l8-f-scalar ; cd:communicativeRole cd:FormulaRole ; cd:selectionPath "cd:latex" ; cd:authoredResource true .
  ex:l8-item-16-3 a cd:SceneItem ; cd:position 3 ; cd:language "en" ; cd:selectsResource ex:l8-essence-16 ; cd:communicativeRole cd:StatementRole ; cd:selectionPath "cd:body" ; cd:authoredResource true .
  ex:l8-scene-16 a cd:SceneDefinition ; cd:focusConcept ex:l8-linear-regression ; cd:teachingSceneType cd:InterpretationSlide ; cd:narration "Multiply each entry by the same scalar. The first calculation multiplies 1 by 2, and the remaining cells repeat the same operation with 2, 3 and 4. The positions and the shape stay the same. A dimensionless scalar preserves the units of the entries."@en ; cd:hasSceneItem ex:l8-item-16-1, ex:l8-item-16-2, ex:l8-item-16-3 ; cd:authoredResource true .
  ex:l8-scene-16 cd:hasSource ex:l8-source-author .
  ex:l8-item-17-1 a cd:SceneItem ; cd:position 1 ; cd:language "en" ; cd:selectsResource ex:l8-heading-17 ; cd:communicativeRole cd:HeadingRole ; cd:selectionPath "skos:prefLabel@en" ; cd:authoredResource true .
  ex:l8-item-17-3 a cd:SceneItem ; cd:position 2 ; cd:language "en" ; cd:selectsResource ex:l8-f-transpose ; cd:communicativeRole cd:FormulaRole ; cd:selectionPath "cd:latex" ; cd:authoredResource true .
  ex:l8-item-17-4 a cd:SceneItem ; cd:position 3 ; cd:language "en" ; cd:selectsResource ex:l8-essence-17 ; cd:communicativeRole cd:StatementRole ; cd:selectionPath "cd:body" ; cd:authoredResource true .
  ex:l8-scene-17 a cd:SceneDefinition ; cd:focusConcept ex:l8-linear-regression ; cd:teachingSceneType cd:InterpretationSlide ; cd:narration "The first row [1,2,3] becomes the first column and the second row [4,5,6] becomes the second column. Shape two-by-three therefore becomes three-by-two. Transposing twice returns the original matrix. Later X transpose will collect dot products with the columns of X."@en ; cd:hasSceneItem ex:l8-item-17-1, ex:l8-item-17-3, ex:l8-item-17-4 ; cd:authoredResource true .
  ex:l8-scene-17 cd:hasSource ex:l8-source-author .
  ex:l8-item-18-1 a cd:SceneItem ; cd:position 1 ; cd:language "en" ; cd:selectsResource ex:l8-heading-18 ; cd:communicativeRole cd:HeadingRole ; cd:selectionPath "skos:prefLabel@en" ; cd:authoredResource true .
  ex:l8-item-18-2 a cd:SceneItem ; cd:position 2 ; cd:language "en" ; cd:selectsResource ex:l8-f-multiply ; cd:communicativeRole cd:FormulaRole ; cd:selectionPath "cd:latex" ; cd:authoredResource true .
  ex:l8-item-18-3 a cd:SceneItem ; cd:position 3 ; cd:language "en" ; cd:selectsResource ex:l8-essence-18 ; cd:communicativeRole cd:StatementRole ; cd:selectionPath "cd:body" ; cd:authoredResource true .
  ex:l8-scene-18 a cd:SceneDefinition ; cd:focusConcept ex:l8-linear-regression ; cd:teachingSceneType cd:ExplorationSlide ; cd:narration "A matrix with m rows and n columns can multiply one with n rows and p columns. Each output entry needs a complete row and a complete column of equal length. The result has m rows and p columns. As a quick question, a two-by-three times a three-by-four is valid and yields two-by-four; the reverse order is not valid. Use the boxed inner dimensions to check the multiplication."@en ; cd:hasSceneItem ex:l8-item-18-1, ex:l8-item-18-2, ex:l8-item-18-3 ; cd:authoredResource true .
  ex:l8-scene-18 cd:hasSource ex:l8-source-author .
  ex:l8-item-19-1 a cd:SceneItem ; cd:position 1 ; cd:language "en" ; cd:selectsResource ex:l8-heading-19 ; cd:communicativeRole cd:HeadingRole ; cd:selectionPath "skos:prefLabel@en" ; cd:authoredResource true .
  ex:l8-item-19-3 a cd:SceneItem ; cd:position 2 ; cd:language "en" ; cd:selectsResource ex:l8-f-dot ; cd:communicativeRole cd:FormulaRole ; cd:selectionPath "cd:latex" ; cd:authoredResource true .
  ex:l8-item-19-4 a cd:SceneItem ; cd:position 3 ; cd:language "en" ; cd:selectsResource ex:l8-essence-19 ; cd:communicativeRole cd:StatementRole ; cd:selectionPath "cd:body" ; cd:authoredResource true .
  ex:l8-scene-19 a cd:SceneDefinition ; cd:focusConcept ex:l8-linear-regression ; cd:teachingSceneType cd:WorkedCalculationSlide ; cd:narration "Each row of A has three entries and each column of B has three entries. Start with the boxed row and column. Multiply the three matching pairs and add to get 5 in the top-left cell. The other three cells use the three remaining row-column pairs and give 13, 14 and 31. The result has two rows from A and two columns from B."@en ; cd:hasSceneItem ex:l8-item-19-1, ex:l8-item-19-3, ex:l8-item-19-4 ; cd:authoredResource true .
  ex:l8-scene-19 cd:hasSource ex:l8-source-author .
  ex:l8-item-20-1 a cd:SceneItem ; cd:position 1 ; cd:language "en" ; cd:selectsResource ex:l8-heading-20 ; cd:communicativeRole cd:HeadingRole ; cd:selectionPath "skos:prefLabel@en" ; cd:authoredResource true .
  ex:l8-item-20-3 a cd:SceneItem ; cd:position 2 ; cd:language "en" ; cd:selectsResource ex:l8-f-products ; cd:communicativeRole cd:FormulaRole ; cd:selectionPath "cd:latex" ; cd:authoredResource true .
  ex:l8-item-20-4 a cd:SceneItem ; cd:position 3 ; cd:language "en" ; cd:selectsResource ex:l8-essence-20 ; cd:communicativeRole cd:StatementRole ; cd:selectionPath "cd:body" ; cd:authoredResource true .
  ex:l8-scene-20 a cd:SceneDefinition ; cd:focusConcept ex:l8-linear-regression ; cd:teachingSceneType cd:InterpretationSlide ; cd:narration "Use a new pair of two-by-two matrices so both products have the same dimensions. The order still matters: AB and BA have different entries. Noncommutativity is about the operation, not a rounding error. For rectangular matrices one order may not even exist. Do not rearrange matrix factors as though they were scalar numbers."@en ; cd:hasSceneItem ex:l8-item-20-1, ex:l8-item-20-3, ex:l8-item-20-4 ; cd:authoredResource true .
  ex:l8-scene-20 cd:hasSource ex:l8-source-author .
  ex:l8-item-21-1 a cd:SceneItem ; cd:position 1 ; cd:language "en" ; cd:selectsResource ex:l8-heading-21 ; cd:communicativeRole cd:HeadingRole ; cd:selectionPath "skos:prefLabel@en" ; cd:authoredResource true .
  ex:l8-item-21-3 a cd:SceneItem ; cd:position 2 ; cd:language "en" ; cd:selectsResource ex:l8-f-hadamard ; cd:communicativeRole cd:FormulaRole ; cd:selectionPath "cd:latex" ; cd:authoredResource true .
  ex:l8-item-21-4 a cd:SceneItem ; cd:position 3 ; cd:language "en" ; cd:selectsResource ex:l8-essence-21 ; cd:communicativeRole cd:StatementRole ; cd:selectionPath "cd:body" ; cd:authoredResource true .
  ex:l8-scene-21 a cd:SceneDefinition ; cd:focusConcept ex:l8-linear-regression ; cd:teachingSceneType cd:InterpretationSlide ; cd:narration "Hadamard multiplication combines corresponding entries of equally shaped matrices. For the same A and B it gives rows [5,12] and [21,32]. This is neither AB nor BA. In R, an asterisk is entrywise multiplication and percent-star-percent is matrix multiplication. Keep that distinction when reading model code."@en ; cd:hasSceneItem ex:l8-item-21-1, ex:l8-item-21-3, ex:l8-item-21-4 ; cd:authoredResource true .
  ex:l8-scene-21 cd:hasSource ex:l8-source-author .
  ex:l8-item-22-1 a cd:SceneItem ; cd:position 1 ; cd:language "en" ; cd:selectsResource ex:l8-heading-22 ; cd:communicativeRole cd:HeadingRole ; cd:selectionPath "skos:prefLabel@en" ; cd:authoredResource true .
  ex:l8-item-22-3 a cd:SceneItem ; cd:position 2 ; cd:language "en" ; cd:selectsResource ex:l8-f-inverse ; cd:communicativeRole cd:FormulaRole ; cd:selectionPath "cd:latex" ; cd:authoredResource true .
  ex:l8-item-22-4 a cd:SceneItem ; cd:position 3 ; cd:language "en" ; cd:selectsResource ex:l8-essence-22 ; cd:communicativeRole cd:StatementRole ; cd:selectionPath "cd:body" ; cd:authoredResource true .
  ex:l8-scene-22 a cd:SceneDefinition ; cd:focusConcept ex:l8-linear-regression ; cd:teachingSceneType cd:InterpretationSlide ; cd:narration "For the new example A = [[2,1],[1,1]], the inverse is [[1,−1],[−1,2]]. Check either multiplication order: the diagonal products sum to one and off-diagonal products sum to zero. An inverse is not obtained by taking reciprocals of individual entries. The inverse exists only for nonsingular square matrices."@en ; cd:hasSceneItem ex:l8-item-22-1, ex:l8-item-22-3, ex:l8-item-22-4 ; cd:authoredResource true .
  ex:l8-scene-22 cd:hasSource ex:l8-source-author .
  ex:l8-item-24-1 a cd:SceneItem ; cd:position 1 ; cd:language "en" ; cd:selectsResource ex:l8-heading-24 ; cd:communicativeRole cd:HeadingRole ; cd:selectionPath "skos:prefLabel@en" ; cd:authoredResource true .
  ex:l8-item-24-3 a cd:SceneItem ; cd:position 2 ; cd:language "en" ; cd:selectsResource ex:l8-f-equations ; cd:communicativeRole cd:FormulaRole ; cd:selectionPath "cd:latex" ; cd:authoredResource true .
  ex:l8-item-24-4 a cd:SceneItem ; cd:position 3 ; cd:language "en" ; cd:selectsResource ex:l8-essence-24 ; cd:communicativeRole cd:StatementRole ; cd:selectionPath "cd:body" ; cd:authoredResource true .
  ex:l8-scene-24 a cd:SceneDefinition ; cd:focusConcept ex:l8-linear-regression ; cd:teachingSceneType cd:WorkedCalculationSlide ; cd:narration "The equations 2u1 + u2 = 5 and u1 + u2 = 3 become Au = b with the same inverse example and b = [5,3]. Left-multiply by the inverse to obtain u = [2,1]. Substitute back: 2 times 2 plus 1 equals 5 and 2 plus 1 equals 3. Row equations and the matrix equation describe the same problem."@en ; cd:hasSceneItem ex:l8-item-24-1, ex:l8-item-24-3, ex:l8-item-24-4 ; cd:authoredResource true .
  ex:l8-scene-24 cd:hasSource ex:l8-source-mit .
  ex:l8-item-residual-orthogonality-1 a cd:SceneItem ; cd:position 1 ; cd:language "en" ; cd:selectsResource ex:l8-heading-residual-orthogonality ; cd:communicativeRole cd:HeadingRole ; cd:selectionPath "skos:prefLabel@en" ; cd:authoredResource true .
  ex:l8-item-residual-orthogonality-2 a cd:SceneItem ; cd:position 2 ; cd:language "en" ; cd:selectsResource ex:l8-orthogonality-section ; cd:communicativeRole cd:DerivationRole ; cd:selectionPath "cd:partOfDerivation" ; cd:authoredResource true .
  ex:l8-scene-residual-orthogonality a cd:SceneDefinition ; cd:focusConcept ex:l8-linear-regression ; cd:teachingSceneType cd:DerivationSlide ; cd:narration "Keep the question visible while reading the two rows of the transposed design and the five fitted residuals. Reveal the row–column operation, distinguishing the dimensionless ones from the times. Only the native result stage displays the two sums and their zero values at the previously fitted minimum. The fitted residuals are 0.08, -0.21, 0.20, -0.09, 0.02 mV at times 0, 1, 2, 3, 4 min; both products cancel. Arbitrary errors need not satisfy these conditions. Next, recover the same coefficient solution using the design matrix."@en ; cd:hasSceneItem ex:l8-item-residual-orthogonality-1, ex:l8-item-residual-orthogonality-2 ; cd:hasSource ex:l8-source-author ; dct:references ex:l8-definition-design, ex:l8-definition-residual, ex:l8-direct-conditions, ex:l8-f-fitted ; cd:authoredResource true .
  ex:l8-item-25-1 a cd:SceneItem ; cd:position 1 ; cd:language "en" ; cd:selectsResource ex:l8-heading-25 ; cd:communicativeRole cd:HeadingRole ; cd:selectionPath "skos:prefLabel@en" ; cd:authoredResource true .
  ex:l8-item-25-2 a cd:SceneItem ; cd:position 2 ; cd:language "en" ; cd:selectsResource ex:l8-normal-from-residuals-section ; cd:communicativeRole cd:DerivationRole ; cd:selectionPath "cd:partOfDerivation" ; cd:authoredResource true .
  ex:l8-scene-25 a cd:SceneDefinition ; cd:focusConcept ex:l8-linear-regression ; cd:teachingSceneType cd:DerivationSlide ; cd:narration "At the minimum the coefficient gradient is zero. Divide its equation by two and move X transpose y to the right to obtain the normal equation."@en ; cd:hasSceneItem ex:l8-item-25-1, ex:l8-item-25-2 ; cd:authoredResource true .
  ex:l8-scene-25 cd:hasSource ex:l8-source-nist-linear .
  ex:l8-item-26-1 a cd:SceneItem ; cd:position 1 ; cd:language "en" ; cd:selectsResource ex:l8-heading-26 ; cd:communicativeRole cd:HeadingRole ; cd:selectionPath "skos:prefLabel@en" ; cd:authoredResource true .
  ex:l8-item-26-2 a cd:SceneItem ; cd:position 2 ; cd:language "en" ; cd:selectsResource ex:l8-media-design-build ; cd:communicativeRole cd:MediaRole ; cd:selectionPath "cd:uri" ; cd:authoredResource true .
  ex:l8-item-26-3 a cd:SceneItem ; cd:position 3 ; cd:language "en" ; cd:selectsResource ex:l8-essence-26 ; cd:communicativeRole cd:StatementRole ; cd:selectionPath "cd:body" ; cd:revealOn ex:l8-media-design-build ; cd:revealAtStage 3 ; cd:authoredResource true .
  ex:l8-scene-26 a cd:SceneDefinition ; cd:focusConcept ex:l8-linear-regression ; cd:teachingSceneType cd:ChapterSlide ; cd:narration "The design matrix records what we assume the response can depend on. Rows keep the observation order; columns record known model terms. These columns encode the model terms used to fit the coefficients. Start with the constant-plus-time model, retaining exactly the same drift dataset."@en ; cd:hasSceneItem ex:l8-item-26-1, ex:l8-item-26-2, ex:l8-item-26-3 ; cd:authoredResource true .
  ex:l8-scene-26 cd:hasSource ex:l8-source-author .
  ex:l8-item-27-1 a cd:SceneItem ; cd:position 1 ; cd:language "en" ; cd:selectsResource ex:l8-heading-27 ; cd:communicativeRole cd:HeadingRole ; cd:selectionPath "skos:prefLabel@en" ; cd:authoredResource true .
  ex:l8-item-27-3 a cd:SceneItem ; cd:position 2 ; cd:language "en" ; cd:selectsResource ex:l8-f-row ; cd:communicativeRole cd:FormulaRole ; cd:selectionPath "cd:latex" ; cd:authoredResource true .
  ex:l8-item-27-4 a cd:SceneItem ; cd:position 3 ; cd:language "en" ; cd:selectsResource ex:l8-essence-27 ; cd:communicativeRole cd:StatementRole ; cd:selectionPath "cd:body" ; cd:authoredResource true .
  ex:l8-scene-27 a cd:SceneDefinition ; cd:focusConcept ex:l8-linear-regression ; cd:teachingSceneType cd:InterpretationSlide ; cd:narration "At the third observation the time is 2 min and the measured signal is 5.20 mV. Its design row is [1,2]: one for the intercept and the observed time for the slope term. The signal is not inserted into X; it remains the matching entry of y. Read this row together with the matching response from the preceding design build."@en ; cd:hasSceneItem ex:l8-item-27-1, ex:l8-item-27-3, ex:l8-item-27-4 ; cd:authoredResource true .
  ex:l8-scene-27 cd:hasSource ex:l8-source-author .
  ex:l8-item-28-1 a cd:SceneItem ; cd:position 1 ; cd:language "en" ; cd:selectsResource ex:l8-heading-28 ; cd:communicativeRole cd:HeadingRole ; cd:selectionPath "skos:prefLabel@en" ; cd:authoredResource true .
  ex:l8-item-28-3 a cd:SceneItem ; cd:position 2 ; cd:language "en" ; cd:selectsResource ex:l8-f-design ; cd:communicativeRole cd:FormulaRole ; cd:selectionPath "cd:latex" ; cd:authoredResource true .
  ex:l8-item-28-4 a cd:SceneItem ; cd:position 3 ; cd:language "en" ; cd:selectsResource ex:l8-essence-28 ; cd:communicativeRole cd:StatementRole ; cd:selectionPath "cd:body" ; cd:authoredResource true .
  ex:l8-scene-28 a cd:SceneDefinition ; cd:focusConcept ex:l8-linear-regression ; cd:teachingSceneType cd:InterpretationSlide ; cd:narration "The first design column consists of five ones, allowing a common intercept. The second contains 0,1,2,3,4 min. Coefficients must be ordered intercept then slope. Swapping columns is permissible only if the coefficient order changes with them. The design definition is graph-owned and separate from its illustrated construction."@en ; cd:hasSceneItem ex:l8-item-28-1, ex:l8-item-28-3, ex:l8-item-28-4 ; cd:authoredResource true .
  ex:l8-scene-28 cd:hasSource ex:l8-source-author .
  ex:l8-item-29-1 a cd:SceneItem ; cd:position 1 ; cd:language "en" ; cd:selectsResource ex:l8-heading-29 ; cd:communicativeRole cd:HeadingRole ; cd:selectionPath "skos:prefLabel@en" ; cd:authoredResource true .
  ex:l8-item-29-3 a cd:SceneItem ; cd:position 2 ; cd:language "en" ; cd:selectsResource ex:l8-f-prediction ; cd:communicativeRole cd:FormulaRole ; cd:selectionPath "cd:latex" ; cd:authoredResource true .
  ex:l8-item-29-4 a cd:SceneItem ; cd:position 3 ; cd:language "en" ; cd:selectsResource ex:l8-essence-29 ; cd:communicativeRole cd:StatementRole ; cd:selectionPath "cd:body" ; cd:authoredResource true .
  ex:l8-scene-29 a cd:SceneDefinition ; cd:focusConcept ex:l8-linear-regression ; cd:teachingSceneType cd:InterpretationSlide ; cd:narration "A five-by-two X multiplies a two-by-one coefficient column to give a five-by-one prediction column. The third row computes intercept plus 2 min times slope. Repeat for all rows without changing the coefficients between observations. This is the same row-dot-column multiplication as the small numerical example."@en ; cd:hasSceneItem ex:l8-item-29-1, ex:l8-item-29-3, ex:l8-item-29-4 ; cd:authoredResource true .
  ex:l8-scene-29 cd:hasSource ex:l8-source-author .
  ex:l8-item-30-1 a cd:SceneItem ; cd:position 1 ; cd:language "en" ; cd:selectsResource ex:l8-heading-30 ; cd:communicativeRole cd:HeadingRole ; cd:selectionPath "skos:prefLabel@en" ; cd:authoredResource true .
  ex:l8-item-30-2 a cd:SceneItem ; cd:position 2 ; cd:language "en" ; cd:selectsResource ex:l8-f-units ; cd:communicativeRole cd:FormulaRole ; cd:selectionPath "cd:latex" ; cd:authoredResource true .
  ex:l8-item-30-3 a cd:SceneItem ; cd:position 3 ; cd:language "en" ; cd:selectsResource ex:l8-essence-30 ; cd:communicativeRole cd:StatementRole ; cd:selectionPath "cd:body" ; cd:authoredResource true .
  ex:l8-scene-30 a cd:SceneDefinition ; cd:focusConcept ex:l8-linear-regression ; cd:teachingSceneType cd:WorkedCalculationSlide ; cd:narration "The constant column is dimensionless; the time column has unit min. Therefore the intercept coefficient needs mV and the slope coefficient mV/min. With the fitted values, the third prediction is 1.02 mV plus 2 min times 1.99 mV/min, giving 5.00 mV. A coefficient column is an ordered collection and its entries need not have identical units."@en ; cd:hasSceneItem ex:l8-item-30-1, ex:l8-item-30-2, ex:l8-item-30-3 ; cd:authoredResource true .
  ex:l8-scene-30 cd:hasSource ex:l8-source-author .
  ex:l8-item-31-1 a cd:SceneItem ; cd:position 1 ; cd:language "en" ; cd:selectsResource ex:l8-heading-31 ; cd:communicativeRole cd:HeadingRole ; cd:selectionPath "skos:prefLabel@en" ; cd:authoredResource true .
  ex:l8-item-31-2 a cd:SceneItem ; cd:position 2 ; cd:language "en" ; cd:selectsResource ex:l8-direct-solve ; cd:communicativeRole cd:FormulaRole ; cd:selectionPath "cd:latex" ; cd:authoredResource true .
  ex:l8-item-31-3 a cd:SceneItem ; cd:position 3 ; cd:language "en" ; cd:selectsResource ex:l8-essence-31 ; cd:communicativeRole cd:StatementRole ; cd:selectionPath "cd:body" ; cd:authoredResource true .
  ex:l8-scene-31 a cd:SceneDefinition ; cd:focusConcept ex:l8-linear-regression ; cd:teachingSceneType cd:DerivationSlide ; cd:narration "Start with M times the fitted coefficient column equals r. If M is invertible, multiply both sides on the left by its inverse. The inverse times M becomes I, so only the coefficient column remains on the left."@en ; cd:hasSceneItem ex:l8-item-31-1, ex:l8-item-31-2, ex:l8-item-31-3 ; cd:authoredResource true .
  ex:l8-scene-31 cd:hasSource ex:l8-source-author .
  ex:l8-item-32-1 a cd:SceneItem ; cd:position 1 ; cd:language "en" ; cd:selectsResource ex:l8-heading-32 ; cd:communicativeRole cd:HeadingRole ; cd:selectionPath "skos:prefLabel@en" ; cd:authoredResource true .
  ex:l8-item-32-2 a cd:SceneItem ; cd:position 2 ; cd:language "en" ; cd:selectsResource ex:l8-residual-column-formula ; cd:communicativeRole cd:FormulaRole ; cd:selectionPath "cd:latex" ; cd:authoredResource true .
  ex:l8-item-32-3 a cd:SceneItem ; cd:position 3 ; cd:language "en" ; cd:selectsResource ex:l8-essence-32 ; cd:communicativeRole cd:StatementRole ; cd:selectionPath "cd:body" ; cd:authoredResource true .
  ex:l8-scene-32 a cd:SceneDefinition ; cd:focusConcept ex:l8-linear-regression ; cd:teachingSceneType cd:DerivationSlide ; cd:narration "Recall the five-point example. Each row of X times the coefficient column gives one prediction. Here the measured y is already known. Subtract the predicted value for each row and call the resulting column e. We use beta for the same coefficient column we previously called b."@en ; cd:hasSceneItem ex:l8-item-32-1, ex:l8-item-32-2, ex:l8-item-32-3 ; cd:authoredResource true .
  ex:l8-scene-32 cd:hasSource ex:l8-source-nist-ls .
  ex:l8-item-33-1 a cd:SceneItem ; cd:position 1 ; cd:language "en" ; cd:selectsResource ex:l8-heading-33 ; cd:communicativeRole cd:HeadingRole ; cd:selectionPath "skos:prefLabel@en" ; cd:authoredResource true .
  ex:l8-scene-33 a cd:SceneDefinition ; cd:focusConcept ex:l8-linear-regression ; cd:teachingSceneType cd:ChapterSlide ; cd:narration "Return from matrix algebra to the five detector readings. We know what to minimise. Now we have the tools to find the coefficients."@en ; cd:hasSceneItem ex:l8-item-33-1 ; cd:authoredResource true .
  ex:l8-scene-33 cd:hasSource ex:l8-source-author .
  ex:l8-item-34-1 a cd:SceneItem ; cd:position 1 ; cd:language "en" ; cd:selectsResource ex:l8-heading-34 ; cd:communicativeRole cd:HeadingRole ; cd:selectionPath "skos:prefLabel@en" ; cd:authoredResource true .
  ex:l8-item-34-2 a cd:SceneItem ; cd:position 2 ; cd:language "en" ; cd:selectsResource ex:l8-minimum-two-coefficients-formula ; cd:communicativeRole cd:FormulaRole ; cd:selectionPath "cd:latex" ; cd:authoredResource true .
  ex:l8-item-34-3 a cd:SceneItem ; cd:position 3 ; cd:language "en" ; cd:selectsResource ex:l8-essence-34 ; cd:communicativeRole cd:StatementRole ; cd:selectionPath "cd:body" ; cd:revealOn ex:l8-heading-34 ; cd:revealAtStage 1 ; cd:authoredResource true .
  ex:l8-scene-34 a cd:SceneDefinition ; cd:focusConcept ex:l8-linear-regression ; cd:teachingSceneType cd:DerivationSlide ; cd:narration "We return to the same five detector readings and the same line. Q is the squared-error score. When either coefficient changes, dQ describes the first-order change in that score. At the minimum, dQ is zero for every change of the two coefficients. Before differentiating in matrix notation, reveal the term inside the square brackets and read it as measured minus predicted signal for one row."@en ; cd:hasSceneItem ex:l8-item-34-1, ex:l8-item-34-2, ex:l8-item-34-3 ; cd:authoredResource true .
  ex:l8-scene-34 cd:hasSource ex:l8-source-nist-ls .
  ex:l8-item-35-1 a cd:SceneItem ; cd:position 1 ; cd:language "en" ; cd:selectsResource ex:l8-heading-35 ; cd:communicativeRole cd:HeadingRole ; cd:selectionPath "skos:prefLabel@en" ; cd:authoredResource true .
  ex:l8-item-35-2 a cd:SceneItem ; cd:position 2 ; cd:language "en" ; cd:selectsResource ex:l8-matrix-squared-error-section ; cd:communicativeRole cd:DerivationRole ; cd:selectionPath "cd:partOfDerivation" ; cd:authoredResource true .
  ex:l8-scene-35 a cd:SceneDefinition ; cd:focusConcept ex:l8-linear-regression ; cd:teachingSceneType cd:DerivationSlide ; cd:narration "Apply the column rule to e. Replace both copies of e by y minus X beta. If we open the transpose on the left, subtraction stays in place and the product X beta reverses to beta transpose times X transpose."@en ; cd:hasSceneItem ex:l8-item-35-1, ex:l8-item-35-2 ; cd:authoredResource true .
  ex:l8-scene-35 cd:hasSource ex:l8-source-author .
  ex:l8-item-36-1 a cd:SceneItem ; cd:position 1 ; cd:language "en" ; cd:selectsResource ex:l8-heading-36 ; cd:communicativeRole cd:HeadingRole ; cd:selectionPath "skos:prefLabel@en" ; cd:authoredResource true .
  ex:l8-item-36-2 a cd:SceneItem ; cd:position 2 ; cd:language "en" ; cd:selectsResource ex:l8-matrix-differential-section ; cd:communicativeRole cd:DerivationRole ; cd:selectionPath "cd:partOfDerivation" ; cd:authoredResource true .
  ex:l8-scene-36 a cd:SceneDefinition ; cd:focusConcept ex:l8-linear-regression ; cd:teachingSceneType cd:DerivationSlide ; cd:narration "Only beta varies. The observed squared length is constant, and the mixed term is linear in beta. Differentiate them one at a time and leave the quadratic derivative for the next slide."@en ; cd:hasSceneItem ex:l8-item-36-1, ex:l8-item-36-2 ; cd:authoredResource true .
  ex:l8-scene-36 cd:hasSource ex:l8-source-author .
  ex:l8-item-37-1 a cd:SceneItem ; cd:position 1 ; cd:language "en" ; cd:selectsResource ex:l8-heading-37 ; cd:communicativeRole cd:HeadingRole ; cd:selectionPath "skos:prefLabel@en" ; cd:authoredResource true .
  ex:l8-item-37-2 a cd:SceneItem ; cd:position 2 ; cd:language "en" ; cd:selectsResource ex:l8-direct-numbers ; cd:communicativeRole cd:FormulaRole ; cd:selectionPath "cd:latex" ; cd:authoredResource true .
  ex:l8-item-37-3 a cd:SceneItem ; cd:position 3 ; cd:language "en" ; cd:selectsResource ex:l8-essence-37 ; cd:communicativeRole cd:StatementRole ; cd:selectionPath "cd:body" ; cd:authoredResource true .
  ex:l8-scene-37 a cd:SceneDefinition ; cd:focusConcept ex:l8-linear-regression ; cd:teachingSceneType cd:WorkedCalculationSlide ; cd:narration "Return to the five detector readings. Use M for X transpose X and r for X transpose y. The entries of these products are the count, the time sums and the time-signal sum shown here. Use M and r as shorter names for the numerical calculation."@en ; cd:hasSceneItem ex:l8-item-37-1, ex:l8-item-37-2, ex:l8-item-37-3 ; cd:authoredResource true .
  ex:l8-scene-37 cd:hasSource ex:l8-source-author .
  ex:l8-item-38-1 a cd:SceneItem ; cd:position 1 ; cd:language "en" ; cd:selectsResource ex:l8-heading-38 ; cd:communicativeRole cd:HeadingRole ; cd:selectionPath "skos:prefLabel@en" ; cd:authoredResource true .
  ex:l8-item-38-2 a cd:SceneItem ; cd:position 2 ; cd:language "en" ; cd:selectsResource ex:l8-direct-inverse ; cd:communicativeRole cd:FormulaRole ; cd:selectionPath "cd:latex" ; cd:authoredResource true .
  ex:l8-item-38-3 a cd:SceneItem ; cd:position 3 ; cd:language "en" ; cd:selectsResource ex:l8-essence-38 ; cd:communicativeRole cd:StatementRole ; cd:selectionPath "cd:body" ; cd:authoredResource true .
  ex:l8-scene-38 a cd:SceneDefinition ; cd:focusConcept ex:l8-linear-regression ; cd:teachingSceneType cd:WorkedCalculationSlide ; cd:narration "Compute the determinant of M. It is 50 in the chosen numerical coordinates, so the inverse exists. Swap the two diagonal entries, negate the off-diagonal entries and divide by 50."@en ; cd:hasSceneItem ex:l8-item-38-1, ex:l8-item-38-2, ex:l8-item-38-3 ; cd:authoredResource true .
  ex:l8-scene-38 cd:hasSource ex:l8-source-author .
  ex:l8-item-39-1 a cd:SceneItem ; cd:position 1 ; cd:language "en" ; cd:selectsResource ex:l8-heading-39 ; cd:communicativeRole cd:HeadingRole ; cd:selectionPath "skos:prefLabel@en" ; cd:authoredResource true .
  ex:l8-item-39-2 a cd:SceneItem ; cd:position 2 ; cd:language "en" ; cd:selectsResource ex:l8-direct-fitted ; cd:communicativeRole cd:FormulaRole ; cd:selectionPath "cd:latex" ; cd:authoredResource true .
  ex:l8-item-39-3 a cd:SceneItem ; cd:position 3 ; cd:language "en" ; cd:selectsResource ex:l8-essence-39 ; cd:communicativeRole cd:StatementRole ; cd:selectionPath "cd:body" ; cd:authoredResource true .
  ex:l8-scene-39 a cd:SceneDefinition ; cd:focusConcept ex:l8-linear-regression ; cd:teachingSceneType cd:WorkedCalculationSlide ; cd:narration "Multiply the inverse of M by r. The fitted intercept is 1.02 mV and the fitted slope is 1.99 mV/min. The fitted line predicts 5.995 mV at 2.5 minutes, answering the opening question."@en ; cd:hasSceneItem ex:l8-item-39-1, ex:l8-item-39-2, ex:l8-item-39-3 ; cd:authoredResource true .
  ex:l8-scene-39 cd:hasSource ex:l8-source-author .
  ex:l8-item-40-1 a cd:SceneItem ; cd:position 1 ; cd:language "en" ; cd:selectsResource ex:l8-heading-40 ; cd:communicativeRole cd:HeadingRole ; cd:selectionPath "skos:prefLabel@en" ; cd:authoredResource true .
  ex:l8-item-40-2 a cd:SceneItem ; cd:position 2 ; cd:language "en" ; cd:selectsResource ex:l8-media-drift-residuals ; cd:communicativeRole cd:MediaRole ; cd:selectionPath "cd:uri" ; cd:authoredResource true .
  ex:l8-item-40-3 a cd:SceneItem ; cd:position 3 ; cd:language "en" ; cd:selectsResource ex:l8-f-fitted ; cd:communicativeRole cd:FormulaRole ; cd:selectionPath "cd:latex" ; cd:authoredResource true .
  ex:l8-item-40-4 a cd:SceneItem ; cd:position 4 ; cd:language "en" ; cd:selectsResource ex:l8-essence-40 ; cd:communicativeRole cd:StatementRole ; cd:selectionPath "cd:body" ; cd:revealOn ex:l8-media-drift-residuals ; cd:revealAtStage 2 ; cd:authoredResource true .
  ex:l8-scene-40 a cd:SceneDefinition ; cd:focusConcept ex:l8-linear-regression ; cd:teachingSceneType cd:WorkedCalculationSlide ; cd:narration "The fitted column is [1.02,3.01,5.00,6.99,8.98] mV. Subtracting it from the unchanged response column gives [0.08,−0.21,0.20,−0.09,0.02] mV. The signed sum and time-weighted sum are both zero to numerical precision, while the squared sum is 0.099 mV². This confirms the normal-equation calculation and distinguishes a fitted line from an exact interpolating curve."@en ; cd:hasSceneItem ex:l8-item-40-1, ex:l8-item-40-2, ex:l8-item-40-3, ex:l8-item-40-4 ; cd:authoredResource true .
  ex:l8-scene-40 cd:hasSource ex:l8-source-author .
  ex:l8-item-41-1 a cd:SceneItem ; cd:position 1 ; cd:language "en" ; cd:selectsResource ex:l8-heading-41 ; cd:communicativeRole cd:HeadingRole ; cd:selectionPath "skos:prefLabel@en" ; cd:authoredResource true .
  ex:l8-item-41-2 a cd:SceneItem ; cd:position 2 ; cd:language "en" ; cd:selectsResource ex:l8-media-dependent-columns ; cd:communicativeRole cd:MediaRole ; cd:selectionPath "cd:uri" ; cd:authoredResource true .
  ex:l8-item-41-3 a cd:SceneItem ; cd:position 3 ; cd:language "en" ; cd:selectsResource ex:l8-f-rank ; cd:communicativeRole cd:FormulaRole ; cd:selectionPath "cd:latex" ; cd:authoredResource true .
  ex:l8-item-41-4 a cd:SceneItem ; cd:position 4 ; cd:language "en" ; cd:selectsResource ex:l8-essence-41 ; cd:communicativeRole cd:StatementRole ; cd:selectionPath "cd:body" ; cd:revealOn ex:l8-media-dependent-columns ; cd:revealAtStage 1 ; cd:authoredResource true .
  ex:l8-scene-41 a cd:SceneDefinition ; cd:focusConcept ex:l8-linear-regression ; cd:teachingSceneType cd:InterpretationSlide ; cd:narration "For p coefficient columns, full column rank means rank(X) = p. If a second constant column is appended, increasing one constant coefficient and decreasing the other by the same amount leaves every prediction unchanged. X transpose X is then singular and coefficient values are not unique. More rows do not repair duplicate columns. For the drift design, the time column is not a multiple of the constant column, so both coefficients are identified."@en ; cd:hasSceneItem ex:l8-item-41-1, ex:l8-item-41-2, ex:l8-item-41-3, ex:l8-item-41-4 ; cd:authoredResource true .
  ex:l8-scene-41 cd:hasSource ex:l8-source-author .
  ex:l8-item-42-1 a cd:SceneItem ; cd:position 1 ; cd:language "en" ; cd:selectsResource ex:l8-heading-42 ; cd:communicativeRole cd:HeadingRole ; cd:selectionPath "skos:prefLabel@en" ; cd:authoredResource true .
  ex:l8-item-42-2 a cd:SceneItem ; cd:position 2 ; cd:language "en" ; cd:selectsResource ex:l8-r-code ; cd:communicativeRole cd:CodeRole ; cd:selectionPath "cd:hasCodeExample" ; cd:authoredResource true .
  ex:l8-item-42-3 a cd:SceneItem ; cd:position 3 ; cd:language "en" ; cd:selectsResource ex:l8-essence-42 ; cd:communicativeRole cd:StatementRole ; cd:selectionPath "cd:body" ; cd:authoredResource true .
  ex:l8-scene-42 a cd:SceneDefinition ; cd:focusConcept ex:l8-linear-regression ; cd:teachingSceneType cd:WorkedCalculationSlide ; cd:narration "The authored code reads: x <- 0:4; y <- c(1.10,2.80,5.20,6.90,9.00); fit <- lm(y ~ x); coef(fit); fitted(fit); residuals(fit); sum(residuals(fit)^2). The tilde describes response by predictor, and lm includes the intercept by default. Expected coefficients are (Intercept) 1.02 and x 1.99; expected SSE is 0.099. model.matrix(fit) shows the columns of ones and x. The function uses a numerically preferable QR-based fit, not our explicit inverse. No external R runtime is needed to read these results; do not introduce summary(fit) inference in this appointment."@en ; cd:hasSceneItem ex:l8-item-42-1, ex:l8-item-42-2, ex:l8-item-42-3 ; cd:authoredResource true .
  ex:l8-scene-42 cd:hasSource ex:l8-source-author .
  ex:l8-item-43-1 a cd:SceneItem ; cd:position 1 ; cd:language "en" ; cd:selectsResource ex:l8-heading-43 ; cd:communicativeRole cd:HeadingRole ; cd:selectionPath "skos:prefLabel@en" ; cd:authoredResource true .
  ex:l8-item-43-2 a cd:SceneItem ; cd:position 2 ; cd:language "en" ; cd:selectsResource ex:l8-media-model-workflow ; cd:communicativeRole cd:MediaRole ; cd:selectionPath "cd:uri" ; cd:authoredResource true .
  ex:l8-item-43-3 a cd:SceneItem ; cd:position 3 ; cd:language "en" ; cd:selectsResource ex:l8-essence-43 ; cd:communicativeRole cd:StatementRole ; cd:selectionPath "cd:body" ; cd:revealOn ex:l8-media-model-workflow ; cd:revealAtStage 3 ; cd:authoredResource true .
  ex:l8-scene-43 a cd:SceneDefinition ; cd:focusConcept ex:l8-linear-regression ; cd:teachingSceneType cd:ChapterSlide ; cd:narration "Applications now use different known terms or a transformed response. Ask what changes in X and what quantity is being minimised. A curved graph can still be linear in coefficients. Log-transforming a response also changes the residual criterion, so it requires a separate explanation."@en ; cd:hasSceneItem ex:l8-item-43-1, ex:l8-item-43-2, ex:l8-item-43-3 ; cd:authoredResource true .
  ex:l8-scene-43 cd:hasSource ex:l8-source-nist-linear .
  ex:l8-item-44-1 a cd:SceneItem ; cd:position 1 ; cd:language "en" ; cd:selectsResource ex:l8-heading-44 ; cd:communicativeRole cd:HeadingRole ; cd:selectionPath "skos:prefLabel@en" ; cd:authoredResource true .
  ex:l8-item-44-2 a cd:SceneItem ; cd:position 2 ; cd:language "en" ; cd:selectsResource ex:l8-fit-quadratic-manual ; cd:communicativeRole cd:ChartRole ; cd:selectionPath "cd:body" ; cd:authoredResource true .
  ex:l8-item-44-3 a cd:SceneItem ; cd:position 3 ; cd:language "en" ; cd:selectsResource ex:l8-essence-44 ; cd:communicativeRole cd:StatementRole ; cd:selectionPath "cd:body" ; cd:authoredResource true .
  ex:l8-scene-44 a cd:SceneDefinition ; cd:focusConcept ex:l8-linear-regression ; cd:teachingSceneType cd:UseCaseSlide ; cd:narration "The new synthetic heating data use times 0,1,2,3,4 min and temperatures 20.98,22.34,25.20,29.66,35.82 °C. In the manual quadratic experiment, begin with an intercept of 20 °C, a time coefficient of 2 °C/min and a squared-time coefficient of 0 °C/min². Ask learners what changes as the squared-time coefficient moves. Compare curves with the same fixed observations and keep the automatic fitted coefficients for the later result scene."@en ; cd:hasSceneItem ex:l8-item-44-1, ex:l8-item-44-2, ex:l8-item-44-3 ; cd:authoredResource true .
  ex:l8-scene-44 cd:hasSource ex:l8-source-author .
  ex:l8-scene-44 dct:references ex:l8-fit-quadratic-manual .
  ex:l8-item-45-1 a cd:SceneItem ; cd:position 1 ; cd:language "en" ; cd:selectsResource ex:l8-heading-45 ; cd:communicativeRole cd:HeadingRole ; cd:selectionPath "skos:prefLabel@en" ; cd:authoredResource true .
  ex:l8-item-45-2 a cd:SceneItem ; cd:position 2 ; cd:language "en" ; cd:selectsResource ex:l8-f-qdesign ; cd:communicativeRole cd:FormulaRole ; cd:selectionPath "cd:latex" ; cd:authoredResource true .
  ex:l8-item-45-3 a cd:SceneItem ; cd:position 3 ; cd:language "en" ; cd:selectsResource ex:l8-essence-45 ; cd:communicativeRole cd:StatementRole ; cd:selectionPath "cd:body" ; cd:authoredResource true .
  ex:l8-scene-45 a cd:SceneDefinition ; cd:focusConcept ex:l8-linear-regression ; cd:teachingSceneType cd:InterpretationSlide ; cd:narration "The design now has five rows and three columns. The third column is 0,1,4,9,16 min², computed from the measured times before fitting. Coefficients are ordered constant, time, squared time. The temperature model is beta0 plus beta1 times x plus beta2 times x squared. Squaring the known predictor does not square an unknown coefficient."@en ; cd:hasSceneItem ex:l8-item-45-1, ex:l8-item-45-2, ex:l8-item-45-3 ; cd:authoredResource true .
  ex:l8-scene-45 cd:hasSource ex:l8-source-author .
  ex:l8-item-46-1 a cd:SceneItem ; cd:position 1 ; cd:language "en" ; cd:selectsResource ex:l8-heading-46 ; cd:communicativeRole cd:HeadingRole ; cd:selectionPath "skos:prefLabel@en" ; cd:authoredResource true .
  ex:l8-item-46-2 a cd:SceneItem ; cd:position 2 ; cd:language "en" ; cd:selectsResource ex:l8-fit-quadratic-auto ; cd:communicativeRole cd:ChartRole ; cd:selectionPath "cd:body" ; cd:authoredResource true .
  ex:l8-item-46-3 a cd:SceneItem ; cd:position 3 ; cd:language "en" ; cd:selectsResource ex:l8-f-qfit ; cd:communicativeRole cd:FormulaRole ; cd:selectionPath "cd:latex" ; cd:authoredResource true .
  ex:l8-item-46-4 a cd:SceneItem ; cd:position 4 ; cd:language "en" ; cd:selectsResource ex:l8-essence-46 ; cd:communicativeRole cd:StatementRole ; cd:selectionPath "cd:body" ; cd:authoredResource true .
  ex:l8-scene-46 a cd:SceneDefinition ; cd:focusConcept ex:l8-linear-regression ; cd:teachingSceneType cd:WorkedCalculationSlide ; cd:narration "The quadratic least-squares coefficients are 21 °C, 0.5 °C/min and 0.8 °C/min². Predictions are 21.00,22.30,25.20,29.70,35.80 °C; residuals are −0.02,+0.04,0,−0.04,+0.02 °C and SSE is 0.004 °C². For comparison, the fitted straight line has intercept 19.4 °C and slope 3.7 °C/min with SSE 8.964 °C². Adding a term cannot increase training SSE when the original columns remain available; a smaller training score alone is not a universal model-selection rule."@en ; cd:hasSceneItem ex:l8-item-46-1, ex:l8-item-46-2, ex:l8-item-46-3, ex:l8-item-46-4 ; cd:authoredResource true .
  ex:l8-scene-46 cd:hasSource ex:l8-source-author .
  ex:l8-scene-46 dct:references ex:l8-fit-quadratic-auto .
  ex:l8-item-47-1 a cd:SceneItem ; cd:position 1 ; cd:language "en" ; cd:selectsResource ex:l8-heading-47 ; cd:communicativeRole cd:HeadingRole ; cd:selectionPath "skos:prefLabel@en" ; cd:authoredResource true .
  ex:l8-item-47-2 a cd:SceneItem ; cd:position 2 ; cd:language "en" ; cd:selectsResource ex:l8-f-quadratic ; cd:communicativeRole cd:FormulaRole ; cd:selectionPath "cd:latex" ; cd:authoredResource true .
  ex:l8-item-47-3 a cd:SceneItem ; cd:position 3 ; cd:language "en" ; cd:selectsResource ex:l8-essence-47 ; cd:communicativeRole cd:StatementRole ; cd:selectionPath "cd:body" ; cd:authoredResource true .
  ex:l8-scene-47 a cd:SceneDefinition ; cd:focusConcept ex:l8-linear-regression ; cd:teachingSceneType cd:InterpretationSlide ; cd:narration "Each unknown coefficient multiplies one known column and the resulting contributions are added. The quadratic model therefore remains a linear coefficient problem. In contrast, an unknown decay constant inside an exponential cannot be treated as a fixed design term on the raw response scale. This definition is about the original specified coefficient representation, not about whether a graph looks straight."@en ; cd:hasSceneItem ex:l8-item-47-1, ex:l8-item-47-2, ex:l8-item-47-3 ; cd:authoredResource true .
  ex:l8-scene-47 cd:hasSource ex:l8-source-nist-linear .
  ex:l8-item-48-1 a cd:SceneItem ; cd:position 1 ; cd:language "en" ; cd:selectsResource ex:l8-heading-48 ; cd:communicativeRole cd:HeadingRole ; cd:selectionPath "skos:prefLabel@en" ; cd:authoredResource true .
  ex:l8-item-48-2 a cd:SceneItem ; cd:position 2 ; cd:language "en" ; cd:selectsResource ex:l8-media-decay-raw ; cd:communicativeRole cd:MediaRole ; cd:selectionPath "cd:uri" ; cd:authoredResource true .
  ex:l8-item-48-3 a cd:SceneItem ; cd:position 3 ; cd:language "en" ; cd:selectsResource ex:l8-f-decay ; cd:communicativeRole cd:FormulaRole ; cd:selectionPath "cd:latex" ; cd:authoredResource true .
  ex:l8-item-48-4 a cd:SceneItem ; cd:position 4 ; cd:language "en" ; cd:selectsResource ex:l8-essence-48 ; cd:communicativeRole cd:StatementRole ; cd:selectionPath "cd:body" ; cd:revealOn ex:l8-media-decay-raw ; cd:revealAtStage 1 ; cd:authoredResource true .
  ex:l8-scene-48 a cd:SceneDefinition ; cd:focusConcept ex:l8-linear-regression ; cd:teachingSceneType cd:UseCaseSlide ; cd:narration "Generate concentration as 20 mg/L times exp(−0.4 per min times t plus epsilon), with dimensionless log perturbations [−0.02,+0.04,0,−0.04,+0.02]. These are synthetic positive concentrations, not the drift signals. Retain the unrounded values from the canonical dataset. The figure shows them on the raw concentration scale; a logarithm will make the specified exponential relation a straight-line coefficient problem."@en ; cd:hasSceneItem ex:l8-item-48-1, ex:l8-item-48-2, ex:l8-item-48-3, ex:l8-item-48-4 ; cd:authoredResource true .
  ex:l8-scene-48 cd:hasSource ex:l8-source-author .
  ex:l8-item-49-1 a cd:SceneItem ; cd:position 1 ; cd:language "en" ; cd:selectsResource ex:l8-heading-49 ; cd:communicativeRole cd:HeadingRole ; cd:selectionPath "skos:prefLabel@en" ; cd:authoredResource true .
  ex:l8-item-49-2 a cd:SceneItem ; cd:position 2 ; cd:language "en" ; cd:selectsResource ex:l8-media-decay-log ; cd:communicativeRole cd:MediaRole ; cd:selectionPath "cd:uri" ; cd:authoredResource true .
  ex:l8-item-49-3 a cd:SceneItem ; cd:position 3 ; cd:language "en" ; cd:selectsResource ex:l8-f-logfit ; cd:communicativeRole cd:FormulaRole ; cd:selectionPath "cd:latex" ; cd:authoredResource true .
  ex:l8-item-49-4 a cd:SceneItem ; cd:position 4 ; cd:language "en" ; cd:selectsResource ex:l8-essence-49 ; cd:communicativeRole cd:StatementRole ; cd:selectionPath "cd:body" ; cd:revealOn ex:l8-media-decay-log ; cd:revealAtStage 1 ; cd:authoredResource true .
  ex:l8-scene-49 a cd:SceneDefinition ; cd:focusConcept ex:l8-linear-regression ; cd:teachingSceneType cd:WorkedCalculationSlide ; cd:narration "Define z as ln(C/C*) with C* fixed at 1 mg/L, so no logarithm is taken of a dimensional quantity. Fit z on time with an intercept. For these perturbations the signed sum and time-weighted sum are both zero, giving intercept ln(20) = 2.995732273553991 and slope −0.4 per min. The log-scale SSE is 0.004 dimensionless. This is a fit to z, not a direct least-squares fit to C."@en ; cd:hasSceneItem ex:l8-item-49-1, ex:l8-item-49-2, ex:l8-item-49-3, ex:l8-item-49-4 ; cd:authoredResource true .
  ex:l8-scene-49 cd:hasSource ex:l8-source-author .
  ex:l8-item-50-1 a cd:SceneItem ; cd:position 1 ; cd:language "en" ; cd:selectsResource ex:l8-heading-50 ; cd:communicativeRole cd:HeadingRole ; cd:selectionPath "skos:prefLabel@en" ; cd:authoredResource true .
  ex:l8-item-50-2 a cd:SceneItem ; cd:position 2 ; cd:language "en" ; cd:selectsResource ex:l8-f-back ; cd:communicativeRole cd:FormulaRole ; cd:selectionPath "cd:latex" ; cd:authoredResource true .
  ex:l8-item-50-3 a cd:SceneItem ; cd:position 3 ; cd:language "en" ; cd:selectsResource ex:l8-essence-50 ; cd:communicativeRole cd:StatementRole ; cd:selectionPath "cd:body" ; cd:authoredResource true .
  ex:l8-scene-50 a cd:SceneDefinition ; cd:focusConcept ex:l8-linear-regression ; cd:teachingSceneType cd:InterpretationSlide ; cd:narration "Exponentiate the fitted log response and multiply by the reference concentration C* to obtain 20 mg/L times exp(−0.4t). This is the back-transformed fitted log response; it is not automatically an unbiased arithmetic mean concentration. The following scene compares the two possible residual criteria explicitly."@en ; cd:hasSceneItem ex:l8-item-50-1, ex:l8-item-50-2, ex:l8-item-50-3 ; cd:authoredResource true .
  ex:l8-scene-50 cd:hasSource ex:l8-source-author .
  ex:l8-item-51-1 a cd:SceneItem ; cd:position 1 ; cd:language "en" ; cd:selectsResource ex:l8-heading-51 ; cd:communicativeRole cd:HeadingRole ; cd:selectionPath "skos:prefLabel@en" ; cd:authoredResource true .
  ex:l8-item-51-2 a cd:SceneItem ; cd:position 2 ; cd:language "en" ; cd:selectsResource ex:l8-fit-reciprocal-auto ; cd:communicativeRole cd:ChartRole ; cd:selectionPath "cd:body" ; cd:authoredResource true .
  ex:l8-item-51-3 a cd:SceneItem ; cd:position 3 ; cd:language "en" ; cd:selectsResource ex:l8-f-reciprocal ; cd:communicativeRole cd:FormulaRole ; cd:selectionPath "cd:latex" ; cd:authoredResource true .
  ex:l8-item-51-4 a cd:SceneItem ; cd:position 4 ; cd:language "en" ; cd:selectsResource ex:l8-essence-51 ; cd:communicativeRole cd:StatementRole ; cd:selectionPath "cd:body" ; cd:authoredResource true .
  ex:l8-scene-51 a cd:SceneDefinition ; cd:focusConcept ex:l8-linear-regression ; cd:teachingSceneType cd:UseCaseSlide ; cd:narration "For positive flow q in mL/min, choose known columns [1,1/q] and fit residence time in min. The illustrative relation is 0.4 min plus 8 mL divided by q. At q = 1,2,4,8,16 mL/min the times are 8.4,4.4,2.4,1.4,0.9 min. The coefficient problem is linear in the two coefficients, even though the curve in q is hyperbolic. Zero flow is excluded. This special reciprocal model does not imply that general saturation models are linear."@en ; cd:hasSceneItem ex:l8-item-51-1, ex:l8-item-51-2, ex:l8-item-51-3, ex:l8-item-51-4 ; cd:authoredResource true .
  ex:l8-scene-51 cd:hasSource ex:l8-source-author .
  ex:l8-scene-51 dct:references ex:l8-fit-reciprocal-auto .
  ex:l8-item-52-1 a cd:SceneItem ; cd:position 1 ; cd:language "en" ; cd:selectsResource ex:l8-heading-52 ; cd:communicativeRole cd:HeadingRole ; cd:selectionPath "skos:prefLabel@en" ; cd:authoredResource true .
  ex:l8-item-52-2 a cd:SceneItem ; cd:position 2 ; cd:language "en" ; cd:selectsResource ex:l8-media-category-design ; cd:communicativeRole cd:MediaRole ; cd:selectionPath "cd:uri" ; cd:authoredResource true .
  ex:l8-item-52-3 a cd:SceneItem ; cd:position 3 ; cd:language "en" ; cd:selectsResource ex:l8-f-anova ; cd:communicativeRole cd:FormulaRole ; cd:selectionPath "cd:latex" ; cd:authoredResource true .
  ex:l8-item-52-4 a cd:SceneItem ; cd:position 4 ; cd:language "en" ; cd:selectsResource ex:l8-essence-52 ; cd:communicativeRole cd:StatementRole ; cd:selectionPath "cd:body" ; cd:revealOn ex:l8-media-category-design ; cd:revealAtStage 1 ; cd:authoredResource true .
  ex:l8-scene-52 a cd:SceneDefinition ; cd:focusConcept ex:l8-linear-regression ; cd:teachingSceneType cd:InterpretationSlide ; cd:narration "Return to the existing Level 7 river-water recovery data for methods A, B and C, each with six observations and means 94%,98%,93%. Choose A as baseline and rows [1,0,0], [1,1,0], [1,0,1] for A,B,C. The coefficients are 94%, +4 percentage points and −1 percentage point; fitted values are the group means and SSE is 30 squared percentage points. This is an encoding bridge only: no F statistic, inference or new ANOVA data are introduced."@en ; cd:hasSceneItem ex:l8-item-52-1, ex:l8-item-52-2, ex:l8-item-52-3, ex:l8-item-52-4 ; cd:authoredResource true .
  ex:l8-scene-52 cd:hasSource ex:l8-source-author .
  ex:l8-item-53-1 a cd:SceneItem ; cd:position 1 ; cd:language "en" ; cd:selectsResource ex:l8-heading-53 ; cd:communicativeRole cd:HeadingRole ; cd:selectionPath "skos:prefLabel@en" ; cd:authoredResource true .
  ex:l8-item-53-2 a cd:SceneItem ; cd:position 2 ; cd:language "en" ; cd:selectsResource ex:l8-media-model-workflow ; cd:communicativeRole cd:MediaRole ; cd:selectionPath "cd:uri" ; cd:authoredResource true .
  ex:l8-item-53-3 a cd:SceneItem ; cd:position 3 ; cd:language "en" ; cd:selectsResource ex:l8-essence-53 ; cd:communicativeRole cd:StatementRole ; cd:selectionPath "cd:body" ; cd:revealOn ex:l8-media-model-workflow ; cd:revealAtStage 3 ; cd:authoredResource true .
  ex:l8-scene-53 a cd:SceneDefinition ; cd:focusConcept ex:l8-linear-regression ; cd:teachingSceneType cd:InterpretationSlide ; cd:narration "Build the known columns, preserve row alignment, fit the coefficients and interpret predictions in the response unit. Straight, quadratic and reciprocal curves differ in known terms; categorical predictors use indicator columns. Log-response fitting changes both the response and the criterion. Full column rank is needed for unique coefficient values. A small training residual score is not the same as a quantified uncertainty or a causal conclusion."@en ; cd:hasSceneItem ex:l8-item-53-1, ex:l8-item-53-2, ex:l8-item-53-3 ; cd:authoredResource true .
  ex:l8-scene-53 cd:hasSource ex:l8-source-author .
  ex:l8-item-54-1 a cd:SceneItem ; cd:position 1 ; cd:language "en" ; cd:selectsResource ex:l8-heading-54 ; cd:communicativeRole cd:HeadingRole ; cd:selectionPath "skos:prefLabel@en" ; cd:authoredResource true .
  ex:l8-item-54-2 a cd:SceneItem ; cd:position 2 ; cd:language "en" ; cd:selectsResource ex:l8-media-drift-observations ; cd:communicativeRole cd:MediaRole ; cd:selectionPath "cd:uri" ; cd:authoredResource true .
  ex:l8-item-54-3 a cd:SceneItem ; cd:position 3 ; cd:language "en" ; cd:selectsResource ex:l8-essence-54 ; cd:communicativeRole cd:StatementRole ; cd:selectionPath "cd:body" ; cd:authoredResource true .
  ex:l8-scene-54 a cd:SceneDefinition ; cd:focusConcept ex:l8-linear-regression ; cd:teachingSceneType cd:ExplorationSlide ; cd:narration "We have computed a fitted line and an interpolation at 2.5 min, but have not quantified uncertainty in coefficients or future responses. Which quantities might change if we repeated the measurements? Leave the question open for the next appointment: today’s fitted values are not yet a quantified statement about their uncertainty."@en ; cd:hasSceneItem ex:l8-item-54-1, ex:l8-item-54-2, ex:l8-item-54-3 ; cd:authoredResource true .
  ex:l8-scene-54 cd:hasSource ex:l8-source-author .
  ex:l8-item-55-1 a cd:SceneItem ; cd:position 1 ; cd:language "en" ; cd:selectsResource ex:l8-heading-55 ; cd:communicativeRole cd:HeadingRole ; cd:selectionPath "skos:prefLabel@en" ; cd:authoredResource true .
  ex:l8-item-55-2 a cd:SceneItem ; cd:position 2 ; cd:language "en" ; cd:selectsResource ex:l8-f-criteria ; cd:communicativeRole cd:FormulaRole ; cd:selectionPath "cd:latex" ; cd:authoredResource true .
  ex:l8-item-55-3 a cd:SceneItem ; cd:position 3 ; cd:language "en" ; cd:selectsResource ex:l8-essence-55 ; cd:communicativeRole cd:StatementRole ; cd:selectionPath "cd:body" ; cd:authoredResource true .
  ex:l8-scene-55 a cd:SceneDefinition ; cd:focusConcept ex:l8-linear-regression ; cd:teachingSceneType cd:InterpretationSlide ; cd:narration "Log-scale least squares minimises squared differences of dimensionless logarithms. Raw-scale least squares instead minimises squared concentration differences in (mg/L)². The fitted log line therefore need not minimise raw concentration SSE. For the authored decay data its log SSE is 0.004, while the raw SSE at the back-transformed log fit is about 0.518628 (mg/L)². Those scores have different units and cannot be ranked against each other. Choose the criterion for the intended measurement model, rather than choosing whichever number is smaller."@en ; cd:hasSceneItem ex:l8-item-55-1, ex:l8-item-55-2, ex:l8-item-55-3 ; cd:authoredResource true .
  ex:l8-scene-55 cd:hasSource ex:l8-source-author .
  ex:l8-five-point-matrix-heading-item a cd:SceneItem ; cd:position 1 ; cd:language "en" ; cd:selectsResource ex:l8-five-point-matrix-heading ; cd:communicativeRole cd:HeadingRole ; cd:selectionPath "skos:prefLabel@en" ; cd:authoredResource true .
  ex:l8-five-point-matrix-math-item a cd:SceneItem ; cd:position 2 ; cd:language "en" ; cd:selectsResource ex:l8-five-point-matrix-section ; cd:communicativeRole cd:DerivationRole ; cd:selectionPath "cd:partOfDerivation" ; cd:authoredResource true .
  ex:l8-five-point-matrix-scene a cd:SceneDefinition ; cd:focusConcept ex:l8-linear-regression ; cd:teachingSceneType cd:WorkedCalculationSlide ; cd:narration "Use the known intercept 2 and slope 0.5. Read the times in the order shown on the slide. Work through the first input 10, then build the whole matrix. The first column of ones carries the intercept into every row and the second column contains the five inputs. Each row times the same coefficient column yields one calculated response. Finally name the three objects X, b and y."@en ; cd:hasSceneItem ex:l8-five-point-matrix-heading-item, ex:l8-five-point-matrix-math-item ; cd:hasSource ex:l8-source-author ; cd:authoredResource true .
  ex:l8-transpose-rules-item-1 a cd:SceneItem ; cd:position 1 ; cd:language "en" ; cd:selectsResource ex:l8-transpose-rules-heading ; cd:communicativeRole cd:HeadingRole ; cd:selectionPath "skos:prefLabel@en" ; cd:authoredResource true .
  ex:l8-transpose-rules-item-2 a cd:SceneItem ; cd:position 2 ; cd:language "en" ; cd:selectsResource ex:l8-transpose-rules-formula ; cd:communicativeRole cd:FormulaRole ; cd:selectionPath "cd:latex" ; cd:authoredResource true .
  ex:l8-transpose-rules-item-3 a cd:SceneItem ; cd:position 3 ; cd:language "en" ; cd:selectsResource ex:l8-transpose-rules-takeaway ; cd:communicativeRole cd:StatementRole ; cd:selectionPath "cd:body" ; cd:authoredResource true .
  ex:l8-transpose-rules-scene a cd:SceneDefinition ; cd:focusConcept ex:l8-linear-regression ; cd:teachingSceneType cd:DerivationSlide ; cd:narration "Subtraction is entrywise, so swapping rows and columns preserves the difference between matching entries. For a product, the row of A and column of B become a column of A transpose and a row of B transpose. Their dot product is preserved by reversing the factors. Transposing a second time swaps the rows and columns back."@en ; cd:hasSceneItem ex:l8-transpose-rules-item-1, ex:l8-transpose-rules-item-2, ex:l8-transpose-rules-item-3 ; cd:hasSource ex:l8-source-author ; cd:authoredResource true .
  ex:l8-column-squares-item-1 a cd:SceneItem ; cd:position 1 ; cd:language "en" ; cd:selectsResource ex:l8-column-squares-heading ; cd:communicativeRole cd:HeadingRole ; cd:selectionPath "skos:prefLabel@en" ; cd:authoredResource true .
  ex:l8-column-squares-item-2 a cd:SceneItem ; cd:position 2 ; cd:language "en" ; cd:selectsResource ex:l8-column-squares-formula ; cd:communicativeRole cd:FormulaRole ; cd:selectionPath "cd:latex" ; cd:authoredResource true .
  ex:l8-column-squares-item-3 a cd:SceneItem ; cd:position 3 ; cd:language "en" ; cd:selectsResource ex:l8-column-squares-takeaway ; cd:communicativeRole cd:StatementRole ; cd:selectionPath "cd:body" ; cd:authoredResource true .
  ex:l8-column-squares-scene a cd:SceneDefinition ; cd:focusConcept ex:l8-linear-regression ; cd:teachingSceneType cd:DerivationSlide ; cd:narration "Transpose the n by 1 column so that it becomes one row. Multiplying that row by the original column pairs each entry with itself and adds the products. For entries 2, 3 and 4 the result is 4 plus 9 plus 16, which is 29."@en ; cd:hasSceneItem ex:l8-column-squares-item-1, ex:l8-column-squares-item-2, ex:l8-column-squares-item-3 ; cd:hasSource ex:l8-source-author ; cd:authoredResource true .
  ex:l8-expand-squared-error-item-1 a cd:SceneItem ; cd:position 1 ; cd:language "en" ; cd:selectsResource ex:l8-expand-squared-error-heading ; cd:communicativeRole cd:HeadingRole ; cd:selectionPath "skos:prefLabel@en" ; cd:authoredResource true .
  ex:l8-expand-squared-error-item-2 a cd:SceneItem ; cd:position 2 ; cd:language "en" ; cd:selectsResource ex:l8-expand-squared-error-section ; cd:communicativeRole cd:DerivationRole ; cd:selectionPath "cd:partOfDerivation" ; cd:authoredResource true .
  ex:l8-expand-squared-error-scene a cd:SceneDefinition ; cd:focusConcept ex:l8-linear-regression ; cd:teachingSceneType cd:DerivationSlide ; cd:narration "Multiply each term in the left bracket by each term in the right bracket, preserving factor order. The mixed products are transposes of one another. Each is a single number, so transposing it does not change its value. This leaves three terms to differentiate."@en ; cd:hasSceneItem ex:l8-expand-squared-error-item-1, ex:l8-expand-squared-error-item-2 ; cd:hasSource ex:l8-source-author ; cd:authoredResource true .
  ex:l8-quadratic-gradient-heading-item a cd:SceneItem ; cd:position 1 ; cd:language "en" ; cd:selectsResource ex:l8-quadratic-gradient-heading ; cd:communicativeRole cd:HeadingRole ; cd:selectionPath "skos:prefLabel@en" ; cd:authoredResource true .
  ex:l8-quadratic-gradient-math-item a cd:SceneItem ; cd:position 2 ; cd:language "en" ; cd:selectsResource ex:l8-quadratic-gradient-section ; cd:communicativeRole cd:DerivationRole ; cd:selectionPath "cd:partOfDerivation" ; cd:authoredResource true .
  ex:l8-quadratic-gradient-scene a cd:SceneDefinition ; cd:focusConcept ex:l8-linear-regression ; cd:teachingSceneType cd:DerivationSlide ; cd:narration "Use the product rule on the two copies of beta. Then use the symmetry of X transpose X to combine their two equal contributions."@en ; cd:hasSceneItem ex:l8-quadratic-gradient-heading-item, ex:l8-quadratic-gradient-math-item ; cd:hasSource ex:l8-source-author ; cd:authoredResource true .
  ex:l8-isolate-coefficients-heading-item a cd:SceneItem ; cd:position 1 ; cd:language "en" ; cd:selectsResource ex:l8-isolate-coefficients-heading ; cd:communicativeRole cd:HeadingRole ; cd:selectionPath "skos:prefLabel@en" ; cd:authoredResource true .
  ex:l8-isolate-coefficients-math-item a cd:SceneItem ; cd:position 2 ; cd:language "en" ; cd:selectsResource ex:l8-isolate-coefficients-section ; cd:communicativeRole cd:DerivationRole ; cd:selectionPath "cd:partOfDerivation" ; cd:authoredResource true .
  ex:l8-isolate-coefficients-scene a cd:SceneDefinition ; cd:focusConcept ex:l8-linear-regression ; cd:teachingSceneType cd:DerivationSlide ; cd:narration "Left-multiply both sides by the inverse of X transpose X. The inverse and its matrix become the identity, leaving the fitted coefficient column on the left."@en ; cd:hasSceneItem ex:l8-isolate-coefficients-heading-item, ex:l8-isolate-coefficients-math-item ; cd:hasSource ex:l8-source-author ; cd:authoredResource true .
  ex:l8-least-squares-solution-item-1 a cd:SceneItem ; cd:position 1 ; cd:language "en" ; cd:selectsResource ex:l8-least-squares-solution-heading ; cd:communicativeRole cd:HeadingRole ; cd:selectionPath "skos:prefLabel@en" ; cd:authoredResource true .
  ex:l8-least-squares-solution-item-2 a cd:SceneItem ; cd:position 2 ; cd:language "en" ; cd:selectsResource ex:l8-least-squares-solution-formula ; cd:communicativeRole cd:FormulaRole ; cd:selectionPath "cd:latex" ; cd:authoredResource true .
  ex:l8-least-squares-solution-item-3 a cd:SceneItem ; cd:position 3 ; cd:language "en" ; cd:selectsResource ex:l8-least-squares-solution-takeaway ; cd:communicativeRole cd:StatementRole ; cd:selectionPath "cd:body" ; cd:authoredResource true .
  ex:l8-least-squares-solution-scene a cd:SceneDefinition ; cd:focusConcept ex:l8-linear-regression ; cd:teachingSceneType cd:InterpretationSlide ; cd:narration "Pause at the result. X encodes the model terms, and y contains the observations. Together they determine the least-squares coefficients when the design columns are independent. Next, examine how the chosen model terms build X and what X transpose X contains."@en ; cd:hasSceneItem ex:l8-least-squares-solution-item-1, ex:l8-least-squares-solution-item-2, ex:l8-least-squares-solution-item-3 ; cd:hasSource ex:l8-source-nist-ls ; cd:authoredResource true .
  ex:l8-basis-linear-item-1 a cd:SceneItem ; cd:position 1 ; cd:language "en" ; cd:selectsResource ex:l8-basis-linear-heading ; cd:communicativeRole cd:HeadingRole ; cd:selectionPath "skos:prefLabel@en" ; cd:authoredResource true .
  ex:l8-basis-linear-item-2 a cd:SceneItem ; cd:position 2 ; cd:language "en" ; cd:selectsResource ex:l8-basis-linear-media ; cd:communicativeRole cd:MediaRole ; cd:selectionPath "cd:uri" ; cd:authoredResource true .
  ex:l8-basis-linear-item-3 a cd:SceneItem ; cd:position 3 ; cd:language "en" ; cd:selectsResource ex:l8-basis-linear-takeaway ; cd:communicativeRole cd:StatementRole ; cd:selectionPath "cd:body" ; cd:authoredResource true .
  ex:l8-basis-linear-scene a cd:SceneDefinition ; cd:focusConcept ex:l8-linear-regression ; cd:teachingSceneType cd:InterpretationSlide ; cd:narration "Read one row as b₀ + b₁xᵢ. For all five inputs, the equations stack into Xb. The first column is x⁰ = 1, including the intercept entry at x = 0. The second column is x itself."@en ; cd:hasSceneItem ex:l8-basis-linear-item-1, ex:l8-basis-linear-item-2, ex:l8-basis-linear-item-3 ; cd:hasSource ex:l8-source-author ; cd:authoredResource true .
  ex:l8-basis-square-item-1 a cd:SceneItem ; cd:position 1 ; cd:language "en" ; cd:selectsResource ex:l8-basis-square-heading ; cd:communicativeRole cd:HeadingRole ; cd:selectionPath "skos:prefLabel@en" ; cd:authoredResource true .
  ex:l8-basis-square-item-2 a cd:SceneItem ; cd:position 2 ; cd:language "en" ; cd:selectsResource ex:l8-basis-square-media ; cd:communicativeRole cd:MediaRole ; cd:selectionPath "cd:uri" ; cd:authoredResource true .
  ex:l8-basis-square-item-3 a cd:SceneItem ; cd:position 3 ; cd:language "en" ; cd:selectsResource ex:l8-basis-square-takeaway ; cd:communicativeRole cd:StatementRole ; cd:selectionPath "cd:body" ; cd:authoredResource true .
  ex:l8-basis-square-scene a cd:SceneDefinition ; cd:focusConcept ex:l8-linear-regression ; cd:teachingSceneType cd:InterpretationSlide ; cd:narration "Keep the constant column and square every input in the second column. This column multiplies b₂. There is no b₁ term. The parabola has its vertex at x = 0; only its right side is shown."@en ; cd:hasSceneItem ex:l8-basis-square-item-1, ex:l8-basis-square-item-2, ex:l8-basis-square-item-3 ; cd:hasSource ex:l8-source-author ; cd:authoredResource true .
  ex:l8-basis-quadratic-item-1 a cd:SceneItem ; cd:position 1 ; cd:language "en" ; cd:selectsResource ex:l8-basis-quadratic-heading ; cd:communicativeRole cd:HeadingRole ; cd:selectionPath "skos:prefLabel@en" ; cd:authoredResource true .
  ex:l8-basis-quadratic-item-2 a cd:SceneItem ; cd:position 2 ; cd:language "en" ; cd:selectsResource ex:l8-basis-quadratic-media ; cd:communicativeRole cd:MediaRole ; cd:selectionPath "cd:uri" ; cd:authoredResource true .
  ex:l8-basis-quadratic-item-3 a cd:SceneItem ; cd:position 3 ; cd:language "en" ; cd:selectsResource ex:l8-basis-quadratic-takeaway ; cd:communicativeRole cd:StatementRole ; cd:selectionPath "cd:body" ; cd:authoredResource true .
  ex:l8-basis-quadratic-scene a cd:SceneDefinition ; cd:focusConcept ex:l8-linear-regression ; cd:teachingSceneType cd:InterpretationSlide ; cd:narration "Keep both transformed columns. The x term tilts the parabola and shifts its vertex. Higher powers x³ and x⁴ are further columns if the model calls for them."@en ; cd:hasSceneItem ex:l8-basis-quadratic-item-1, ex:l8-basis-quadratic-item-2, ex:l8-basis-quadratic-item-3 ; cd:hasSource ex:l8-source-author ; cd:authoredResource true .
  ex:l8-basis-hyperbolic-item-1 a cd:SceneItem ; cd:position 1 ; cd:language "en" ; cd:selectsResource ex:l8-basis-hyperbolic-heading ; cd:communicativeRole cd:HeadingRole ; cd:selectionPath "skos:prefLabel@en" ; cd:authoredResource true .
  ex:l8-basis-hyperbolic-item-2 a cd:SceneItem ; cd:position 2 ; cd:language "en" ; cd:selectsResource ex:l8-basis-hyperbolic-media ; cd:communicativeRole cd:MediaRole ; cd:selectionPath "cd:uri" ; cd:authoredResource true .
  ex:l8-basis-hyperbolic-item-3 a cd:SceneItem ; cd:position 3 ; cd:language "en" ; cd:selectsResource ex:l8-basis-hyperbolic-takeaway ; cd:communicativeRole cd:StatementRole ; cd:selectionPath "cd:body" ; cd:authoredResource true .
  ex:l8-basis-hyperbolic-scene a cd:SceneDefinition ; cd:focusConcept ex:l8-linear-regression ; cd:teachingSceneType cd:InterpretationSlide ; cd:narration "Use dimensionless x. The sinh column changes sign across zero, while cosh has the same value at x and minus x. Their weights are independent. These are hyperbolic functions; a reciprocal term is a different way to obtain a hyperbola."@en ; cd:hasSceneItem ex:l8-basis-hyperbolic-item-1, ex:l8-basis-hyperbolic-item-2, ex:l8-basis-hyperbolic-item-3 ; cd:hasSource ex:l8-source-author ; cd:authoredResource true .
  ex:l8-basis-exp-item-1 a cd:SceneItem ; cd:position 1 ; cd:language "en" ; cd:selectsResource ex:l8-basis-exp-heading ; cd:communicativeRole cd:HeadingRole ; cd:selectionPath "skos:prefLabel@en" ; cd:authoredResource true .
  ex:l8-basis-exp-item-2 a cd:SceneItem ; cd:position 2 ; cd:language "en" ; cd:selectsResource ex:l8-basis-exp-media ; cd:communicativeRole cd:MediaRole ; cd:selectionPath "cd:uri" ; cd:authoredResource true .
  ex:l8-basis-exp-item-3 a cd:SceneItem ; cd:position 3 ; cd:language "en" ; cd:selectsResource ex:l8-basis-exp-takeaway ; cd:communicativeRole cd:StatementRole ; cd:selectionPath "cd:body" ; cd:authoredResource true .
  ex:l8-basis-exp-scene a cd:SceneDefinition ; cd:focusConcept ex:l8-linear-regression ; cd:teachingSceneType cd:InterpretationSlide ; cd:narration "Exponentiate each dimensionless input before fitting. The multiplier of exp(x) is a coefficient. If an unknown coefficient were placed inside the exponential, the model would no longer be linear in that coefficient."@en ; cd:hasSceneItem ex:l8-basis-exp-item-1, ex:l8-basis-exp-item-2, ex:l8-basis-exp-item-3 ; cd:hasSource ex:l8-source-author ; cd:authoredResource true .
  ex:l8-basis-log-item-1 a cd:SceneItem ; cd:position 1 ; cd:language "en" ; cd:selectsResource ex:l8-basis-log-heading ; cd:communicativeRole cd:HeadingRole ; cd:selectionPath "skos:prefLabel@en" ; cd:authoredResource true .
  ex:l8-basis-log-item-2 a cd:SceneItem ; cd:position 2 ; cd:language "en" ; cd:selectsResource ex:l8-basis-log-media ; cd:communicativeRole cd:MediaRole ; cd:selectionPath "cd:uri" ; cd:authoredResource true .
  ex:l8-basis-log-item-3 a cd:SceneItem ; cd:position 3 ; cd:language "en" ; cd:selectsResource ex:l8-basis-log-takeaway ; cd:communicativeRole cd:StatementRole ; cd:selectionPath "cd:body" ; cd:authoredResource true .
  ex:l8-basis-log-scene a cd:SceneDefinition ; cd:focusConcept ex:l8-linear-regression ; cd:teachingSceneType cd:InterpretationSlide ; cd:narration "Use positive, dimensionless inputs. The logarithm acts on x, while the response remains on its original scale. This differs from fitting a logarithm of the measured response."@en ; cd:hasSceneItem ex:l8-basis-log-item-1, ex:l8-basis-log-item-2, ex:l8-basis-log-item-3 ; cd:hasSource ex:l8-source-author ; cd:authoredResource true .
  ex:l8-basis-reciprocal-item-1 a cd:SceneItem ; cd:position 1 ; cd:language "en" ; cd:selectsResource ex:l8-basis-reciprocal-heading ; cd:communicativeRole cd:HeadingRole ; cd:selectionPath "skos:prefLabel@en" ; cd:authoredResource true .
  ex:l8-basis-reciprocal-item-2 a cd:SceneItem ; cd:position 2 ; cd:language "en" ; cd:selectsResource ex:l8-basis-reciprocal-media ; cd:communicativeRole cd:MediaRole ; cd:selectionPath "cd:uri" ; cd:authoredResource true .
  ex:l8-basis-reciprocal-item-3 a cd:SceneItem ; cd:position 3 ; cd:language "en" ; cd:selectsResource ex:l8-basis-reciprocal-takeaway ; cd:communicativeRole cd:StatementRole ; cd:selectionPath "cd:body" ; cd:authoredResource true .
  ex:l8-basis-reciprocal-scene a cd:SceneDefinition ; cd:focusConcept ex:l8-linear-regression ; cd:teachingSceneType cd:InterpretationSlide ; cd:narration "Use nonzero x. Here the five inputs are positive and the curve tends toward the intercept. The reciprocal is undefined at zero, so never draw a continuous curve through zero."@en ; cd:hasSceneItem ex:l8-basis-reciprocal-item-1, ex:l8-basis-reciprocal-item-2, ex:l8-basis-reciprocal-item-3 ; cd:hasSource ex:l8-source-author ; cd:authoredResource true .
  ex:l8-basis-sqrt-item-1 a cd:SceneItem ; cd:position 1 ; cd:language "en" ; cd:selectsResource ex:l8-basis-sqrt-heading ; cd:communicativeRole cd:HeadingRole ; cd:selectionPath "skos:prefLabel@en" ; cd:authoredResource true .
  ex:l8-basis-sqrt-item-2 a cd:SceneItem ; cd:position 2 ; cd:language "en" ; cd:selectsResource ex:l8-basis-sqrt-media ; cd:communicativeRole cd:MediaRole ; cd:selectionPath "cd:uri" ; cd:authoredResource true .
  ex:l8-basis-sqrt-item-3 a cd:SceneItem ; cd:position 3 ; cd:language "en" ; cd:selectsResource ex:l8-basis-sqrt-takeaway ; cd:communicativeRole cd:StatementRole ; cd:selectionPath "cd:body" ; cd:authoredResource true .
  ex:l8-basis-sqrt-scene a cd:SceneDefinition ; cd:focusConcept ex:l8-linear-regression ; cd:teachingSceneType cd:InterpretationSlide ; cd:narration "For real-valued square roots, x must be nonnegative. This case uses the same five positive inputs as the exponential, logarithm and reciprocal examples. The transform is fixed before fitting."@en ; cd:hasSceneItem ex:l8-basis-sqrt-item-1, ex:l8-basis-sqrt-item-2, ex:l8-basis-sqrt-item-3 ; cd:hasSource ex:l8-source-author ; cd:authoredResource true .
  ex:l8-basis-gram-columns-item-1 a cd:SceneItem ; cd:position 1 ; cd:language "en" ; cd:selectsResource ex:l8-basis-gram-columns-heading ; cd:communicativeRole cd:HeadingRole ; cd:selectionPath "skos:prefLabel@en" ; cd:authoredResource true .
  ex:l8-basis-gram-columns-item-2 a cd:SceneItem ; cd:position 2 ; cd:language "en" ; cd:selectsResource ex:l8-basis-gram-columns-formula ; cd:communicativeRole cd:FormulaRole ; cd:selectionPath "cd:latex" ; cd:authoredResource true .
  ex:l8-basis-gram-columns-item-3 a cd:SceneItem ; cd:position 3 ; cd:language "en" ; cd:selectsResource ex:l8-basis-gram-columns-takeaway ; cd:communicativeRole cd:StatementRole ; cd:selectionPath "cd:body" ; cd:authoredResource true .
  ex:l8-basis-gram-columns-scene a cd:SceneDefinition ; cd:focusConcept ex:l8-linear-regression ; cd:teachingSceneType cd:DerivationSlide ; cd:narration "Return to the straight line with inputs zero through four. The first column is all ones and the second contains x. Their four pairwise dot products yield 5, 10, 10 and 30. The cross-products match across the diagonal. With more design columns, compare every pair in the same way."@en ; cd:hasSceneItem ex:l8-basis-gram-columns-item-1, ex:l8-basis-gram-columns-item-2, ex:l8-basis-gram-columns-item-3 ; cd:hasSource ex:l8-source-author ; cd:authoredResource true .
  ex:l8-fixed-basis-coefficients-item-1 a cd:SceneItem ; cd:position 1 ; cd:language "en" ; cd:selectsResource ex:l8-fixed-basis-coefficients-heading ; cd:communicativeRole cd:HeadingRole ; cd:selectionPath "skos:prefLabel@en" ; cd:authoredResource true .
  ex:l8-fixed-basis-coefficients-item-2 a cd:SceneItem ; cd:position 2 ; cd:language "en" ; cd:selectsResource ex:l8-fixed-basis-coefficients-formula ; cd:communicativeRole cd:FormulaRole ; cd:selectionPath "cd:latex" ; cd:authoredResource true .
  ex:l8-fixed-basis-coefficients-item-3 a cd:SceneItem ; cd:position 3 ; cd:language "en" ; cd:selectsResource ex:l8-fixed-basis-coefficients-takeaway ; cd:communicativeRole cd:StatementRole ; cd:selectionPath "cd:body" ; cd:authoredResource true .
  ex:l8-fixed-basis-coefficients-scene a cd:SceneDefinition ; cd:focusConcept ex:l8-linear-regression ; cd:teachingSceneType cd:InterpretationSlide ; cd:narration "A fixed function of x can form a design column even when its curve is nonlinear. In b₄ times sinh(x), b₄ scales a known column. In sinh(x times b₄) or exp(x times b₂), changing a coefficient also changes the column. The exponential of x plus b₂ is different: separate the factors and fit the new multiplier u. Recover b₂ as ln(u) only for positive u. An unconstrained least-squares fit need not satisfy that restriction."@en ; cd:hasSceneItem ex:l8-fixed-basis-coefficients-item-1, ex:l8-fixed-basis-coefficients-item-2, ex:l8-fixed-basis-coefficients-item-3 ; cd:hasSource ex:l8-source-author ; cd:authoredResource true .
  ex:l8-basis-mixed-item-1 a cd:SceneItem ; cd:position 1 ; cd:language "en" ; cd:selectsResource ex:l8-basis-mixed-heading ; cd:communicativeRole cd:HeadingRole ; cd:selectionPath "skos:prefLabel@en" ; cd:authoredResource true .
  ex:l8-basis-mixed-item-2 a cd:SceneItem ; cd:position 2 ; cd:language "en" ; cd:selectsResource ex:l8-basis-mixed-media ; cd:communicativeRole cd:MediaRole ; cd:selectionPath "cd:uri" ; cd:authoredResource true .
  ex:l8-basis-mixed-item-3 a cd:SceneItem ; cd:position 3 ; cd:language "en" ; cd:selectsResource ex:l8-basis-mixed-takeaway ; cd:communicativeRole cd:StatementRole ; cd:selectionPath "cd:body" ; cd:authoredResource true .
  ex:l8-basis-mixed-scene a cd:SceneDefinition ; cd:focusConcept ex:l8-linear-regression ; cd:teachingSceneType cd:InterpretationSlide ; cd:narration "These are the first five rows of a design with seven columns. Take z equal to x minus three. The curve uses chosen weights to show how the terms can interact in shape. To estimate seven coefficients uniquely, collect at least seven observations and check that the seven columns are independent. To leave room for estimating error, collect more than seven."@en ; cd:hasSceneItem ex:l8-basis-mixed-item-1, ex:l8-basis-mixed-item-2, ex:l8-basis-mixed-item-3 ; cd:hasSource ex:l8-source-author ; cd:authoredResource true .
  ex:l8-basis-column-limit-item-1 a cd:SceneItem ; cd:position 1 ; cd:language "en" ; cd:selectsResource ex:l8-basis-column-limit-heading ; cd:communicativeRole cd:HeadingRole ; cd:selectionPath "skos:prefLabel@en" ; cd:authoredResource true .
  ex:l8-basis-column-limit-item-2 a cd:SceneItem ; cd:position 2 ; cd:language "en" ; cd:selectsResource ex:l8-basis-column-limit-formula ; cd:communicativeRole cd:FormulaRole ; cd:selectionPath "cd:latex" ; cd:authoredResource true .
  ex:l8-basis-column-limit-item-3 a cd:SceneItem ; cd:position 3 ; cd:language "en" ; cd:selectsResource ex:l8-basis-column-limit-takeaway ; cd:communicativeRole cd:StatementRole ; cd:selectionPath "cd:body" ; cd:authoredResource true .
  ex:l8-basis-column-limit-scene a cd:SceneDefinition ; cd:focusConcept ex:l8-linear-regression ; cd:teachingSceneType cd:InterpretationSlide ; cd:narration "With independent columns, the residual degrees of freedom equal the number of rows minus the number of fitted coefficients. With five rows and four independent columns, one residual direction remains. With five independent columns, the fitted values can match all five observations exactly. There is then no residual degree of freedom for error estimation. Seven columns cannot be independent in five-dimensional observation space."@en ; cd:hasSceneItem ex:l8-basis-column-limit-item-1, ex:l8-basis-column-limit-item-2, ex:l8-basis-column-limit-item-3 ; cd:hasSource ex:l8-source-author ; cd:authoredResource true .
  ex:l8-basis-eight-rows-item-1 a cd:SceneItem ; cd:position 1 ; cd:language "en" ; cd:selectsResource ex:l8-basis-eight-rows-heading ; cd:communicativeRole cd:HeadingRole ; cd:selectionPath "skos:prefLabel@en" ; cd:authoredResource true .
  ex:l8-basis-eight-rows-item-2 a cd:SceneItem ; cd:position 2 ; cd:language "en" ; cd:selectsResource ex:l8-basis-eight-rows-media ; cd:communicativeRole cd:MediaRole ; cd:selectionPath "cd:uri" ; cd:authoredResource true .
  ex:l8-basis-eight-rows-item-3 a cd:SceneItem ; cd:position 3 ; cd:language "en" ; cd:selectsResource ex:l8-basis-eight-rows-takeaway ; cd:communicativeRole cd:StatementRole ; cd:selectionPath "cd:body" ; cd:authoredResource true .
  ex:l8-basis-eight-rows-scene a cd:SceneDefinition ; cd:focusConcept ex:l8-linear-regression ; cd:teachingSceneType cd:InterpretationSlide ; cd:narration "Keep the same seven columns and make three more measurements inside the original input range, at 1.5, 2.5 and 3.5. The resulting design has rank seven at full precision, so eight response values would determine a unique least-squares fit. Only one residual degree of freedom remains. The plotted curve still uses the chosen illustrative coefficients."@en ; cd:hasSceneItem ex:l8-basis-eight-rows-item-1, ex:l8-basis-eight-rows-item-2, ex:l8-basis-eight-rows-item-3 ; cd:hasSource ex:l8-source-author ; cd:authoredResource true .
  ex:l8-gram-design-item-1 a cd:SceneItem ; cd:position 1 ; cd:language "en" ; cd:selectsResource ex:l8-gram-design-heading ; cd:communicativeRole cd:HeadingRole ; cd:selectionPath "skos:prefLabel@en" ; cd:authoredResource true .
  ex:l8-gram-design-item-2 a cd:SceneItem ; cd:position 2 ; cd:language "en" ; cd:selectsResource ex:l8-gram-design-media ; cd:communicativeRole cd:MediaRole ; cd:selectionPath "cd:uri" ; cd:authoredResource true .
  ex:l8-gram-design-item-3 a cd:SceneItem ; cd:position 3 ; cd:language "en" ; cd:selectsResource ex:l8-gram-design-takeaway ; cd:communicativeRole cd:StatementRole ; cd:selectionPath "cd:body" ; cd:authoredResource true .
  ex:l8-gram-design-scene a cd:SceneDefinition ; cd:focusConcept ex:l8-linear-regression ; cd:teachingSceneType cd:InterpretationSlide ; cd:narration "Use the five input values 1, 4, 9, 16 and 25. The columns are the constant one, x itself and the square root of x. The plotted curve is Xb at those inputs and the same model evaluated between them, using chosen coefficients."@en ; cd:hasSceneItem ex:l8-gram-design-item-1, ex:l8-gram-design-item-2, ex:l8-gram-design-item-3 ; cd:hasSource ex:l8-source-author ; cd:authoredResource true .
  ex:l8-gram-rule-item-1 a cd:SceneItem ; cd:position 1 ; cd:language "en" ; cd:selectsResource ex:l8-gram-rule-heading ; cd:communicativeRole cd:HeadingRole ; cd:selectionPath "skos:prefLabel@en" ; cd:authoredResource true .
  ex:l8-gram-rule-item-2 a cd:SceneItem ; cd:position 2 ; cd:language "en" ; cd:selectsResource ex:l8-gram-rule-formula ; cd:communicativeRole cd:FormulaRole ; cd:selectionPath "cd:latex" ; cd:authoredResource true .
  ex:l8-gram-rule-item-3 a cd:SceneItem ; cd:position 3 ; cd:language "en" ; cd:selectsResource ex:l8-gram-rule-takeaway ; cd:communicativeRole cd:StatementRole ; cd:selectionPath "cd:body" ; cd:authoredResource true .
  ex:l8-gram-rule-scene a cd:SceneDefinition ; cd:focusConcept ex:l8-linear-regression ; cd:teachingSceneType cd:InterpretationSlide ; cd:narration "Recall that e transpose e is one dot product of a column with itself. X transpose X applies that rule to every pair of columns. A diagonal entry sums squares of one column. An off-diagonal entry sums products of two different columns in matching rows."@en ; cd:hasSceneItem ex:l8-gram-rule-item-1, ex:l8-gram-rule-item-2, ex:l8-gram-rule-item-3 ; cd:hasSource ex:l8-source-author ; cd:authoredResource true .
  ex:l8-gram-worked-item-1 a cd:SceneItem ; cd:position 1 ; cd:language "en" ; cd:selectsResource ex:l8-gram-worked-heading ; cd:communicativeRole cd:HeadingRole ; cd:selectionPath "skos:prefLabel@en" ; cd:authoredResource true .
  ex:l8-gram-worked-item-2 a cd:SceneItem ; cd:position 2 ; cd:language "en" ; cd:selectsResource ex:l8-gram-worked-formula ; cd:communicativeRole cd:FormulaRole ; cd:selectionPath "cd:latex" ; cd:authoredResource true .
  ex:l8-gram-worked-item-3 a cd:SceneItem ; cd:position 3 ; cd:language "en" ; cd:selectsResource ex:l8-gram-worked-takeaway ; cd:communicativeRole cd:StatementRole ; cd:selectionPath "cd:body" ; cd:authoredResource true .
  ex:l8-gram-worked-scene a cd:SceneDefinition ; cd:focusConcept ex:l8-linear-regression ; cd:teachingSceneType cd:InterpretationSlide ; cd:narration "Read the second column as x and the third as square roots. Multiply matching entries and sum. To get the second diagonal entry, square every x and add. To get entry row two, column three, multiply x by its square root in each row and add. Its mirror entry has the same value. Repeat with the column of ones and the third column to complete the matrix."@en ; cd:hasSceneItem ex:l8-gram-worked-item-1, ex:l8-gram-worked-item-2, ex:l8-gram-worked-item-3 ; cd:hasSource ex:l8-source-author ; cd:authoredResource true .
  ex:l8-xty-worked-item-1 a cd:SceneItem ; cd:position 1 ; cd:language "en" ; cd:selectsResource ex:l8-xty-worked-heading ; cd:communicativeRole cd:HeadingRole ; cd:selectionPath "skos:prefLabel@en" ; cd:authoredResource true .
  ex:l8-xty-worked-item-2 a cd:SceneItem ; cd:position 2 ; cd:language "en" ; cd:selectsResource ex:l8-xty-worked-formula ; cd:communicativeRole cd:FormulaRole ; cd:selectionPath "cd:latex" ; cd:authoredResource true .
  ex:l8-xty-worked-item-3 a cd:SceneItem ; cd:position 3 ; cd:language "en" ; cd:selectsResource ex:l8-xty-worked-takeaway ; cd:communicativeRole cd:StatementRole ; cd:selectionPath "cd:body" ; cd:authoredResource true .
  ex:l8-xty-worked-scene a cd:SceneDefinition ; cd:focusConcept ex:l8-linear-regression ; cd:teachingSceneType cd:InterpretationSlide ; cd:narration "Keep the same five input rows and align the example measurements 2, 3, 5, 6 and 9 with them in order. Multiply each design column entry by the matching measured response and add the five products. The constant column gives the response sum, the x column gives 380, and the square-root column gives 92. This is the right-hand side of the normal equation."@en ; cd:hasSceneItem ex:l8-xty-worked-item-1, ex:l8-xty-worked-item-2, ex:l8-xty-worked-item-3 ; cd:hasSource ex:l8-source-author ; cd:authoredResource true .
  ex:l8-inverse-remaining-item-1 a cd:SceneItem ; cd:position 1 ; cd:language "en" ; cd:selectsResource ex:l8-inverse-remaining-heading ; cd:communicativeRole cd:HeadingRole ; cd:selectionPath "skos:prefLabel@en" ; cd:authoredResource true .
  ex:l8-inverse-remaining-item-2 a cd:SceneItem ; cd:position 2 ; cd:language "en" ; cd:selectsResource ex:l8-inverse-remaining-formula ; cd:communicativeRole cd:FormulaRole ; cd:selectionPath "cd:latex" ; cd:authoredResource true .
  ex:l8-inverse-remaining-item-3 a cd:SceneItem ; cd:position 3 ; cd:language "en" ; cd:selectsResource ex:l8-inverse-remaining-takeaway ; cd:communicativeRole cd:StatementRole ; cd:selectionPath "cd:body" ; cd:authoredResource true .
  ex:l8-inverse-remaining-scene a cd:SceneDefinition ; cd:focusConcept ex:l8-linear-regression ; cd:teachingSceneType cd:InterpretationSlide ; cd:narration "We already have both products. Call X transpose X G and X transpose y r. The inverse notation describes the solution. We can get the same coefficients by solving G beta hat equals r directly."@en ; cd:hasSceneItem ex:l8-inverse-remaining-item-1, ex:l8-inverse-remaining-item-2, ex:l8-inverse-remaining-item-3 ; cd:hasSource ex:l8-source-author ; cd:authoredResource true .
  ex:l8-inverse-methods-item-1 a cd:SceneItem ; cd:position 1 ; cd:language "en" ; cd:selectsResource ex:l8-inverse-methods-heading ; cd:communicativeRole cd:HeadingRole ; cd:selectionPath "skos:prefLabel@en" ; cd:authoredResource true .
  ex:l8-inverse-methods-item-2 a cd:SceneItem ; cd:position 2 ; cd:language "en" ; cd:selectsResource ex:l8-inverse-methods-media ; cd:communicativeRole cd:MediaRole ; cd:selectionPath "cd:uri" ; cd:authoredResource true .
  ex:l8-inverse-methods-item-3 a cd:SceneItem ; cd:position 3 ; cd:language "en" ; cd:selectsResource ex:l8-inverse-methods-takeaway ; cd:communicativeRole cd:StatementRole ; cd:selectionPath "cd:body" ; cd:authoredResource true .
  ex:l8-inverse-methods-item-4 a cd:SceneItem ; cd:position 4 ; cd:language "en" ; cd:selectsResource ex:l8-inverse-methods-ref-determinant ; cd:communicativeRole cd:MediaRole ; cd:selectionPath "cd:uri" ; cd:authoredResource true .
  ex:l8-inverse-methods-item-5 a cd:SceneItem ; cd:position 5 ; cd:language "en" ; cd:selectsResource ex:l8-inverse-methods-ref-cholesky ; cd:communicativeRole cd:MediaRole ; cd:selectionPath "cd:uri" ; cd:authoredResource true .
  ex:l8-inverse-methods-scene a cd:SceneDefinition ; cd:focusConcept ex:l8-linear-regression ; cd:teachingSceneType cd:InterpretationSlide ; cd:narration "For an invertible two-by-two matrix, use the determinant formula. For a symmetric positive-definite matrix, use Cholesky factorisation. Cholesky factors can be used to form the inverse or solve the normal equations directly. Use the references to read more about each method."@en ; cd:hasSceneItem ex:l8-inverse-methods-item-1, ex:l8-inverse-methods-item-2, ex:l8-inverse-methods-item-3, ex:l8-inverse-methods-item-4, ex:l8-inverse-methods-item-5 ; cd:hasSource ex:l8-inverse-methods-source-determinant, ex:l8-inverse-methods-source-cholesky ; cd:authoredResource true .
  ex:l8-drift-prediction-item-1 a cd:SceneItem ; cd:position 1 ; cd:language "en" ; cd:selectsResource ex:l8-drift-prediction-heading ; cd:communicativeRole cd:HeadingRole ; cd:selectionPath "skos:prefLabel@en" ; cd:authoredResource true .
  ex:l8-drift-prediction-item-2 a cd:SceneItem ; cd:position 2 ; cd:language "en" ; cd:selectsResource ex:l8-drift-prediction-media ; cd:communicativeRole cd:MediaRole ; cd:selectionPath "cd:uri" ; cd:authoredResource true .
  ex:l8-drift-prediction-item-3 a cd:SceneItem ; cd:position 3 ; cd:language "en" ; cd:selectsResource ex:l8-drift-prediction-takeaway ; cd:communicativeRole cd:StatementRole ; cd:selectionPath "cd:body" ; cd:revealOn ex:l8-drift-prediction-media ; cd:revealAtStage 1 ; cd:authoredResource true .
  ex:l8-drift-prediction-scene a cd:SceneDefinition ; cd:focusConcept ex:l8-linear-regression ; cd:teachingSceneType cd:InterpretationSlide ; cd:narration "Return to the detector series from the beginning. Fit a line by ordinary least squares to all five readings. The intercept is 1.02 millivolts, and the slope is 1.99 millivolts per minute. At 2.5 minutes, reading the line gives 5.995 millivolts, which is about 6 millivolts. This time lies between two measured times, so the prediction is an interpolation."@en ; cd:hasSceneItem ex:l8-drift-prediction-item-1, ex:l8-drift-prediction-item-2, ex:l8-drift-prediction-item-3 ; cd:hasSource ex:l8-source-author ; cd:authoredResource true .
  ex:l8-drift-fit-item-1 a cd:SceneItem ; cd:position 1 ; cd:language "en" ; cd:selectsResource ex:l8-drift-fit-heading ; cd:communicativeRole cd:HeadingRole ; cd:selectionPath "skos:prefLabel@en" ; cd:authoredResource true .
  ex:l8-drift-fit-item-2 a cd:SceneItem ; cd:position 2 ; cd:language "en" ; cd:selectsResource ex:l8-drift-fit-formula ; cd:communicativeRole cd:FormulaRole ; cd:selectionPath "cd:latex" ; cd:authoredResource true .
  ex:l8-drift-fit-item-3 a cd:SceneItem ; cd:position 3 ; cd:language "en" ; cd:selectsResource ex:l8-drift-fit-takeaway ; cd:communicativeRole cd:StatementRole ; cd:selectionPath "cd:body" ; cd:authoredResource true .
  ex:l8-drift-fit-scene a cd:SceneDefinition ; cd:focusConcept ex:l8-linear-regression ; cd:teachingSceneType cd:WorkedCalculationSlide ; cd:narration "Use the five original measurements at times zero through four. The columns of X are ones and time. Their cross-products give X transpose X, and their products with the measured readings give X transpose y. Apply the two-by-two inverse using determinant 50. Multiplying by the response cross-products yields the intercept 1.02 and slope 1.99."@en ; cd:hasSceneItem ex:l8-drift-fit-item-1, ex:l8-drift-fit-item-2, ex:l8-drift-fit-item-3 ; cd:hasSource ex:l8-source-author ; cd:authoredResource true .
  ex:l8-drift-products-item-1 a cd:SceneItem ; cd:position 1 ; cd:language "en" ; cd:selectsResource ex:l8-drift-products-heading ; cd:communicativeRole cd:HeadingRole ; cd:selectionPath "skos:prefLabel@en" ; cd:authoredResource true .
  ex:l8-drift-products-item-2 a cd:SceneItem ; cd:position 2 ; cd:language "en" ; cd:selectsResource ex:l8-drift-products-media ; cd:communicativeRole cd:MediaRole ; cd:selectionPath "cd:uri" ; cd:authoredResource true .
  ex:l8-drift-products-scene a cd:SceneDefinition ; cd:focusConcept ex:l8-linear-regression ; cd:teachingSceneType cd:WorkedCalculationSlide ; cd:narration "Start with the five time and signal pairs. The first design column contains ones for the intercept. For X transpose X, pair the design columns with each other. The ones with themselves give 5, the ones with time give 10 in both off-diagonal entries, and time with itself gives 30. For X transpose y, pair each design column with the observed signals. The ones give 25 and the time-weighted sum gives 69.9."@en ; cd:hasSceneItem ex:l8-drift-products-item-1, ex:l8-drift-products-item-2 ; cd:hasSource ex:l8-source-author ; cd:authoredResource true .
  ex:l8-heating-straight-check-item-1 a cd:SceneItem ; cd:position 1 ; cd:language "en" ; cd:selectsResource ex:l8-heating-straight-check-heading ; cd:communicativeRole cd:HeadingRole ; cd:selectionPath "skos:prefLabel@en" ; cd:authoredResource true .
  ex:l8-heating-straight-check-item-2 a cd:SceneItem ; cd:position 2 ; cd:language "en" ; cd:selectsResource ex:l8-heating-straight-check-media ; cd:communicativeRole cd:MediaRole ; cd:selectionPath "cd:uri" ; cd:authoredResource true .
  ex:l8-heating-straight-check-scene a cd:SceneDefinition ; cd:focusConcept ex:l8-linear-regression ; cd:teachingSceneType cd:GuidedObservationSlide ; cd:narration "During a heating ramp, the temperature was recorded once per minute. Ask whether a constant heating rate describes the five observations. Reveal the best straight line, then inspect the vertical residuals. The pattern suggests a changing rate."@en ; cd:hasSceneItem ex:l8-heating-straight-check-item-1, ex:l8-heating-straight-check-item-2 ; cd:hasSource ex:l8-source-author ; cd:authoredResource true .
  ex:l8-heating-quadratic-fit-item-1 a cd:SceneItem ; cd:position 1 ; cd:language "en" ; cd:selectsResource ex:l8-heating-quadratic-fit-heading ; cd:communicativeRole cd:HeadingRole ; cd:selectionPath "skos:prefLabel@en" ; cd:authoredResource true .
  ex:l8-heating-quadratic-fit-item-2 a cd:SceneItem ; cd:position 2 ; cd:language "en" ; cd:selectsResource ex:l8-heating-quadratic-fit-media ; cd:communicativeRole cd:MediaRole ; cd:selectionPath "cd:uri" ; cd:authoredResource true .
  ex:l8-heating-quadratic-fit-scene a cd:SceneDefinition ; cd:focusConcept ex:l8-linear-regression ; cd:teachingSceneType cd:WorkedCalculationSlide ; cd:narration "Each row represents one measurement. Start with the ones for the intercept, add the observed time for the linear term, then square time to get the third column. Fit the three coefficients together with the same least-squares method and compare the two fits."@en ; cd:hasSceneItem ex:l8-heating-quadratic-fit-item-1, ex:l8-heating-quadratic-fit-item-2 ; cd:hasSource ex:l8-source-author ; cd:authoredResource true .
  ex:l8-log-decay-observations-item-1 a cd:SceneItem ; cd:position 1 ; cd:language "en" ; cd:selectsResource ex:l8-log-decay-observations-heading ; cd:communicativeRole cd:HeadingRole ; cd:selectionPath "skos:prefLabel@en" ; cd:authoredResource true .
  ex:l8-log-decay-observations-item-2 a cd:SceneItem ; cd:position 2 ; cd:language "en" ; cd:selectsResource ex:l8-log-decay-observations-media ; cd:communicativeRole cd:MediaRole ; cd:selectionPath "cd:uri" ; cd:authoredResource true .
  ex:l8-log-decay-observations-scene a cd:SceneDefinition ; cd:focusConcept ex:l8-linear-regression ; cd:teachingSceneType cd:UseCaseSlide ; cd:narration "Follow a dissolved tracer sampled once every minute. The drop in concentration is visibly larger at the start. Show the first and last one-minute drops and ask whether the loss is more naturally described as a fraction of what remains."@en ; cd:hasSceneItem ex:l8-log-decay-observations-item-1, ex:l8-log-decay-observations-item-2 ; cd:hasSource ex:l8-source-author ; cd:authoredResource true .
  ex:l8-log-decay-transform-item-1 a cd:SceneItem ; cd:position 1 ; cd:language "en" ; cd:selectsResource ex:l8-log-decay-transform-heading ; cd:communicativeRole cd:HeadingRole ; cd:selectionPath "skos:prefLabel@en" ; cd:authoredResource true .
  ex:l8-log-decay-transform-item-2 a cd:SceneItem ; cd:position 2 ; cd:language "en" ; cd:selectsResource ex:l8-log-decay-transform-formula ; cd:communicativeRole cd:FormulaRole ; cd:selectionPath "cd:latex" ; cd:authoredResource true .
  ex:l8-log-decay-transform-item-3 a cd:SceneItem ; cd:position 3 ; cd:language "en" ; cd:selectsResource ex:l8-log-decay-transform-takeaway ; cd:communicativeRole cd:StatementRole ; cd:selectionPath "cd:body" ; cd:authoredResource true .
  ex:l8-log-decay-transform-scene a cd:SceneDefinition ; cd:focusConcept ex:l8-linear-regression ; cd:teachingSceneType cd:WorkedCalculationSlide ; cd:narration "Time stays in minutes. Divide the positive concentrations by the reference of one milligram per litre, then take the natural log of that unitless ratio. For example, 19.60 milligrams per litre becomes about 2.98. Logarithms turn a ratio between consecutive concentrations into a difference. A common retention factor therefore means a common step on the log scale."@en ; cd:hasSceneItem ex:l8-log-decay-transform-item-1, ex:l8-log-decay-transform-item-2, ex:l8-log-decay-transform-item-3 ; cd:hasSource ex:l8-source-author ; cd:authoredResource true .
  ex:l8-log-decay-fit-item-1 a cd:SceneItem ; cd:position 1 ; cd:language "en" ; cd:selectsResource ex:l8-log-decay-fit-heading ; cd:communicativeRole cd:HeadingRole ; cd:selectionPath "skos:prefLabel@en" ; cd:authoredResource true .
  ex:l8-log-decay-fit-item-2 a cd:SceneItem ; cd:position 2 ; cd:language "en" ; cd:selectsResource ex:l8-log-decay-fit-media ; cd:communicativeRole cd:MediaRole ; cd:selectionPath "cd:uri" ; cd:authoredResource true .
  ex:l8-log-decay-fit-item-3 a cd:SceneItem ; cd:position 3 ; cd:language "en" ; cd:selectsResource ex:l8-log-decay-fit-formula ; cd:communicativeRole cd:FormulaRole ; cd:selectionPath "cd:latex" ; cd:authoredResource true .
  ex:l8-log-decay-fit-scene a cd:SceneDefinition ; cd:focusConcept ex:l8-linear-regression ; cd:teachingSceneType cd:WorkedCalculationSlide ; cd:narration "Fit the line to the five logarithms using an intercept and time. Reveal the result on the left. Then exponentiate the fitted log values and multiply by the reference concentration to return to milligrams per litre. The model retains about 67 percent each minute. Least squares was applied to the log response."@en ; cd:hasSceneItem ex:l8-log-decay-fit-item-1, ex:l8-log-decay-fit-item-2, ex:l8-log-decay-fit-item-3 ; cd:hasSource ex:l8-source-author ; cd:authoredResource true .
  ex:l8-anova-recovery-design-item-1 a cd:SceneItem ; cd:position 1 ; cd:language "en" ; cd:selectsResource ex:l8-anova-recovery-design-heading ; cd:communicativeRole cd:HeadingRole ; cd:selectionPath "skos:prefLabel@en" ; cd:authoredResource true .
  ex:l8-anova-recovery-design-item-2 a cd:SceneItem ; cd:position 2 ; cd:language "en" ; cd:selectsResource ex:l8-anova-recovery-design-media ; cd:communicativeRole cd:MediaRole ; cd:selectionPath "cd:uri" ; cd:authoredResource true .
  ex:l8-anova-recovery-design-scene a cd:SceneDefinition ; cd:focusConcept ex:l8-linear-regression ; cd:teachingSceneType cd:WorkedCalculationSlide ; cd:narration "Return to the eighteen independent river-water SPE preparations from Level 7. Recovery goes in the response vector. Start with the method labels and measurements, then add a column of ones for the intercept. Add one indicator for method B, then one for C. A has zeros in both. With the intercept present, a third method indicator would be redundant."@en ; cd:hasSceneItem ex:l8-anova-recovery-design-item-1, ex:l8-anova-recovery-design-item-2 ; cd:hasSource ex:l8-source-author ; cd:authoredResource true .
  ex:l8-anova-recovery-fit-item-1 a cd:SceneItem ; cd:position 1 ; cd:language "en" ; cd:selectsResource ex:l8-anova-recovery-fit-heading ; cd:communicativeRole cd:HeadingRole ; cd:selectionPath "skos:prefLabel@en" ; cd:authoredResource true .
  ex:l8-anova-recovery-fit-item-2 a cd:SceneItem ; cd:position 2 ; cd:language "en" ; cd:selectsResource ex:l8-anova-recovery-fit-media ; cd:communicativeRole cd:MediaRole ; cd:selectionPath "cd:uri" ; cd:authoredResource true .
  ex:l8-anova-recovery-fit-item-3 a cd:SceneItem ; cd:position 3 ; cd:language "en" ; cd:selectsResource ex:l8-anova-recovery-fit-formula ; cd:communicativeRole cd:FormulaRole ; cd:selectionPath "cd:latex" ; cd:authoredResource true .
  ex:l8-anova-recovery-fit-scene a cd:SceneDefinition ; cd:focusConcept ex:l8-linear-regression ; cd:teachingSceneType cd:WorkedCalculationSlide ; cd:narration "With just the intercept, we predict the same recovery for all samples: 95 percent. With the dummy columns, the fitted intercept is 94 percent and the method adjustments are plus four and minus one percentage points. Predicted values are the three group means. The reduction of 84 in residual sum of squares costs two degrees of freedom; divide that mean square by the residual mean square to recover the same F of 21 as in Level 7."@en ; cd:hasSceneItem ex:l8-anova-recovery-fit-item-1, ex:l8-anova-recovery-fit-item-2, ex:l8-anova-recovery-fit-item-3 ; cd:hasSource ex:l8-source-author ; cd:authoredResource true .
  ex:l8-multiple-regression-design-item-1 a cd:SceneItem ; cd:position 1 ; cd:language "en" ; cd:selectsResource ex:l8-multiple-regression-design-heading ; cd:communicativeRole cd:HeadingRole ; cd:selectionPath "skos:prefLabel@en" ; cd:authoredResource true .
  ex:l8-multiple-regression-design-item-2 a cd:SceneItem ; cd:position 2 ; cd:language "en" ; cd:selectsResource ex:l8-multiple-regression-design-media ; cd:communicativeRole cd:MediaRole ; cd:selectionPath "cd:uri" ; cd:authoredResource true .
  ex:l8-multiple-regression-design-scene a cd:SceneDefinition ; cd:focusConcept ex:l8-linear-regression ; cd:teachingSceneType cd:WorkedCalculationSlide ; cd:narration "In this teaching example, prepare three concentration standards and measure each at 20 and 30 degrees Celsius. How can one regression account for both settings? Keep one row per measurement. Add the column of ones, the measured concentration, and temperature minus the 20 degree reference. Temperature centring shifts the intercept without changing the fitted values."@en ; cd:hasSceneItem ex:l8-multiple-regression-design-item-1, ex:l8-multiple-regression-design-item-2 ; cd:hasSource ex:l8-source-author ; cd:authoredResource true .
  ex:l8-multiple-regression-fit-item-1 a cd:SceneItem ; cd:position 1 ; cd:language "en" ; cd:selectsResource ex:l8-multiple-regression-fit-heading ; cd:communicativeRole cd:HeadingRole ; cd:selectionPath "skos:prefLabel@en" ; cd:authoredResource true .
  ex:l8-multiple-regression-fit-item-2 a cd:SceneItem ; cd:position 2 ; cd:language "en" ; cd:selectsResource ex:l8-multiple-regression-fit-media ; cd:communicativeRole cd:MediaRole ; cd:selectionPath "cd:uri" ; cd:authoredResource true .
  ex:l8-multiple-regression-fit-item-3 a cd:SceneItem ; cd:position 3 ; cd:language "en" ; cd:selectsResource ex:l8-multiple-regression-fit-formula ; cd:communicativeRole cd:FormulaRole ; cd:selectionPath "cd:latex" ; cd:authoredResource true .
  ex:l8-multiple-regression-fit-scene a cd:SceneDefinition ; cd:focusConcept ex:l8-linear-regression ; cd:teachingSceneType cd:WorkedCalculationSlide ; cd:narration "Fit both predictors together with ordinary least squares. At fixed temperature the fitted signal rises two millivolts per milligram per litre. At fixed concentration it rises one millivolt for ten degrees Celsius. The profiles are parallel because this model assigns the same concentration slope at both temperatures. In the next example, replace measurements in the design columns with zero and one to represent a categorical method."@en ; cd:hasSceneItem ex:l8-multiple-regression-fit-item-1, ex:l8-multiple-regression-fit-item-2, ex:l8-multiple-regression-fit-item-3 ; cd:hasSource ex:l8-source-author ; cd:authoredResource true .
  ex:l8-multiple-regression-products-item-1 a cd:SceneItem ; cd:position 1 ; cd:language "en" ; cd:selectsResource ex:l8-multiple-regression-products-heading ; cd:communicativeRole cd:HeadingRole ; cd:selectionPath "skos:prefLabel@en" ; cd:authoredResource true .
  ex:l8-multiple-regression-products-item-2 a cd:SceneItem ; cd:position 2 ; cd:language "en" ; cd:selectsResource ex:l8-multiple-regression-products-media ; cd:communicativeRole cd:MediaRole ; cd:selectionPath "cd:uri" ; cd:authoredResource true .
  ex:l8-multiple-regression-products-item-3 a cd:SceneItem ; cd:position 3 ; cd:language "en" ; cd:selectsResource ex:l8-multiple-regression-products-formula ; cd:communicativeRole cd:FormulaRole ; cd:selectionPath "cd:latex" ; cd:authoredResource true .
  ex:l8-multiple-regression-products-scene a cd:SceneDefinition ; cd:focusConcept ex:l8-linear-regression ; cd:teachingSceneType cd:WorkedCalculationSlide ; cd:narration "Start from the same six rows. Pair design columns to build X transpose X, adding products down the rows. The entries above and below the diagonal match. For X transpose y, pair each design column with the measured signals instead."@en ; cd:hasSceneItem ex:l8-multiple-regression-products-item-1, ex:l8-multiple-regression-products-item-2, ex:l8-multiple-regression-products-item-3 ; cd:hasSource ex:l8-source-author ; cd:authoredResource true .
  ex:l8-multiple-regression-coefficients-item-1 a cd:SceneItem ; cd:position 1 ; cd:language "en" ; cd:selectsResource ex:l8-multiple-regression-coefficients-heading ; cd:communicativeRole cd:HeadingRole ; cd:selectionPath "skos:prefLabel@en" ; cd:authoredResource true .
  ex:l8-multiple-regression-coefficients-item-2 a cd:SceneItem ; cd:position 2 ; cd:language "en" ; cd:selectsResource ex:l8-multiple-regression-coefficients-formula ; cd:communicativeRole cd:FormulaRole ; cd:selectionPath "cd:latex" ; cd:authoredResource true .
  ex:l8-multiple-regression-coefficients-item-3 a cd:SceneItem ; cd:position 3 ; cd:language "en" ; cd:selectsResource ex:l8-multiple-regression-coefficients-takeaway ; cd:communicativeRole cd:StatementRole ; cd:selectionPath "cd:body" ; cd:authoredResource true .
  ex:l8-multiple-regression-coefficients-scene a cd:SceneDefinition ; cd:focusConcept ex:l8-linear-regression ; cd:teachingSceneType cd:WorkedCalculationSlide ; cd:narration "Substitute the three-by-three matrix and the three-entry signal cross-product vector in the coefficient formula. The result is an intercept of one millivolt, a concentration slope of two millivolts per milligram per litre, and a temperature slope of one tenth of a millivolt per degree."@en ; cd:hasSceneItem ex:l8-multiple-regression-coefficients-item-1, ex:l8-multiple-regression-coefficients-item-2, ex:l8-multiple-regression-coefficients-item-3 ; cd:hasSource ex:l8-source-author ; cd:authoredResource true .
}
